{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog","id":936233,"title":"Mechanical Errata OPP Blog","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T14:05:48-07:00","id":936233,"title":"Mechanical Errata OPP Blog","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/awakening-2e-errata-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/awakening-2e-errata-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Awakening 2e Errata [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/awakening-2e-errata-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/awakening-2e-errata-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Haven't read yet, posted so people who don't follow the main page can find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:13:28-07:00","id":936237,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see that a number of my suggestions got through. The changes to starting Rotes is also nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:21:56-07:00","id":936240,"title":"","content":"Man, a lot of great changes in here. I'm a little bummed about Temporal Sympathy, but it's probably for the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:43:17-07:00","id":936248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936237#post936237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changes to starting Rotes is also nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to feel about it. It's a significant buff for specialists, but also a significant nerf for generalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:11:36-07:00","id":936266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936248#post936248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to feel about it. It's a significant buff for specialists, but also a significant nerf for generalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is consistent with 2e's flat-cost pricing model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:30:48-07:00","id":936273,"title":"","content":"It was mostly the inconsistency between starting Rotes being dot-based but bought Rotes being flat. Starting with six one-dot rotes and then buying two three-dot Rotes with your first two Arcane Experiences was outright better than the reverse (it saved you an entire Arcanum dot's worth of Arcane XP, in fact).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T16:14:06-07:00","id":936292,"title":"","content":"Im hype for zombie change. Too tired to comment on rest; only thing that made me sad was making Pattern Restoration Instant.<br /> EDIT<br /> And hype for Death/Spirit Armors. And Chaos Mastery (other than chance die option). And...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-23-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T16:58:29-07:00","id":936310,"title":"","content":"Hey, Rotting Flesh is Perfecting. It looks like they went for the model where Death spells that promote decay are Perfecting, and those that inhibit it are Fraying, since Death is the arcanum of decay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T17:40:04-07:00","id":936320,"title":"","content":"I am <i>exceedingly pleased</i> by the changes to Mental Shield, considering how incredibly situational the original version was.<br /> <br /> &quot;Protects against one additional source per additional Reach&quot; was preposterous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:07:38-07:00","id":936361,"title":"","content":"And Space was (relatively) untouched!<br /> <br /> This pleases me greatly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:24:39-07:00","id":936364,"title":"","content":"Well, it looks like there are a few spells I'll need to review with regards to my Legacy conversions. That said, can anyone clarify this tidbit for me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E Errata</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Automatic Activation: Attainments gain primary ranks equal to dots in the Arcanum *minus one*, and secondary factor penalties *up to* the Arcanum&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming the 'secondary factor penalties' refer to being able to customize the secondary spell factors for the Legacy Attainments on a situational basis?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:50:43-07:00","id":936376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936364#post936364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming the 'secondary factor penalties' refer to being able to customize the secondary spell factors for the Legacy Attainments on a situational basis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be a clarification, but from what it seems like to me, you basically can get up to 4 primary factor ranks automatically and to determine secondary factor ranks you can take up to 4 dice penalties (Or 2 ranks)[Technically you could take up to 5 dice penalties, but since that 5th removed die doesn't do anything...] Factors, I think, have always been able to be customized to some extent since they automatically increase as your ranks in an arcana grow at the very least. I don't see why inside the limitations of attainments in their fairly fixed nature you couldn't customize them on a situational basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T20:59:21-07:00","id":936400,"title":"","content":"&quot; ... you can't combine two attack spells to do two sets of damage, but you can combine two attack spells to do one set of damage and spend reach on two different secondary effects those attack spells might have. &quot; I am most happy for this line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:26:09-07:00","id":936406,"title":"","content":"<b>Temporal Sympathy:</b> Only works on time spells that call for it or other spells combined with a suitable time spell.<br /> <br /> I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:53:23-07:00","id":936418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have changed the creative thaumaturgy rules to reflect direct attacks not always being<br /> <br /> Fraying or Unraveling and Healing not always being Perfecting and Patterning. </div> </div> </div><br /> Yay! Consistency of terminology wins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Transmission: can change the frequency. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-24-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T00:48:10-07:00","id":936448,"title":"","content":"Also very happy about Fate clarifications. And for the Proximi buff. As raw before they were pretty much stuck as ritualistic that bugged sometimes. Noone likes getting bugged. And the drawback really hurt. Now they feel very witchy. In a good way. Very much like proper half template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:30:28-07:00","id":936469,"title":"","content":"Relasing Paradox got a very needed buff. Now, when you are facing a small Paradox Pool that might result in one success at most, you might consider Releasing it - 1 Paradox can either modify your Reach (generally, bad) or apply a Condition to the subject of the spell - assuming your Storyteller isn't using all Paradox to undo and cancel your spells, it might be actually desirable to release a paradox targeting something that you don't care too much about. <br /> <br /> It also changes unsafely relinquishing spells a little, as it allows applying conditions to things targeted by the out-of-control spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:36:39-07:00","id":936470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spell stacking applies if the<br /> <br /> constituent spells affect the same thing, which even affects instantaneous results like damage -<br /> <br /> you can't combine two attack spells to do two sets of damage, but you can combine two attack<br /> <br /> spells to do one set of damage and spend reach on two different secondary effects those attack<br /> <br /> spells might have. </div> </div> </div><br /> Does it mean that you can't gank someone and just direct damage him to hell in one turn?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-24-2016, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:52:53-07:00","id":936472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936376#post936376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might be a clarification, but from what it seems like to me, you basically can get up to 4 primary factor ranks automatically and to determine secondary factor ranks you can take up to 4 dice penalties (Or 2 ranks)[Technically you could take up to 5 dice penalties, but since that 5th removed die doesn't do anything...] Factors, I think, have always been able to be customized to some extent since they automatically increase as your ranks in an arcana grow at the very least. I don't see why inside the limitations of attainments in their fairly fixed nature you couldn't customize them on a situational basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not following there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:01:14-07:00","id":936478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Resonant Mana allows the use of a Persona Yantra worth 1 die, it doesn&amp;#39;t increase existing persona yantra sources by 1. (This might not sound like a big difference, but trust me, it works out!) </div> </div> </div>I cannot remember a single reference to Resonant Mana in the entire book. None pops up when I search, either. Is there something I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T04:16:26-07:00","id":936489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SleepyChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936406#post936406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Temporal Sympathy:</b> Only works on time spells that call for it or other spells combined with a suitable time spell.<br /> <br /> I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't fully understand what does this mean and how its a big change from the previous version can someone clarify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T04:31:13-07:00","id":936492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936489#post936489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't fully understand what does this mean and how its a big change from the previous version can someone clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you can't send e.g. Honning the Form two scenes back because its not a time spell. You can however Shift Sands to travel back and then cast Honning the Form on your target in your &quot;present&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:50:55-07:00","id":936506,"title":"","content":"Oh, Opacity is separate for everyone? I felt like I should've understood that, but now that changes a lot for understanding how Mysteries narratively function in-setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:58:38-07:00","id":936510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936472#post936472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not following there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without elaboration on why you think you might be confused it's going to be impossible to try and help you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936492#post936492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you can't send e.g. Honning the Form two scenes back because its not a time spell. You can however Shift Sands to travel back and then cast Honning the Form on your target in your &quot;present&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably also Combine cast Shifting Sands and Honing the Form to send the spell back in time to your target, but that's certainly more balanced than simply being able to send the spell back by itself in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936506#post936506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Opacity is separate for everyone? I felt like I should've understood that, but now that changes a lot for understanding how Mysteries narratively function in-setting</div> </div> </div> </div>It was already separate, what isn't clear is if this removes the effect of Nimbus contamination hiking up the Opacity for everyone or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936478#post936478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot remember a single reference to Resonant Mana in the entire book. None pops up when I search, either. Is there something I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resonance can typically be described by a keyword<br /> that describes an image, emotion, or theme, such as \u201cSubterranean,\u201d<br /> \u201cWrathful,\u201d or \u201cIchthyoid.\u201d When a sorcerer spends Mana from this<br /> tass on a spell where the effect or manifestation matches the stored<br /> Resonance (\u201cIchthyoid\u201d for growing gills, for instance), it suffuses her<br /> Nimbus, providing a +1 persona Yantra bonus. </div> </div> </div> Pg. 242","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-24-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:54:38-07:00","id":936522,"title":"","content":"I'm still bummed by no more Free Reaches in Legacies Attainments... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T07:21:12-07:00","id":936534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SleepyChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936406#post936406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Temporal Sympathy:</b> Only works on time spells that call for it or other spells combined with a suitable time spell.<br /> <br /> I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't. I get why the change was made, Temporal Sympathy would have been kind of bonkers if it could send any spell back in time. But with the errata it's practically useless. There are all of three spells that can be affected by Temporal Sympathy that will ever actually be cast without it: Momentary Flux, Postcognition, and Warp. Every other spell that is affected by Temporal Sympathy is a Time spell at 2 dots or higher, so there will never be a time when you can cast such a spell and can't use Temporal Sympathy with it. With this change, lirerally the only thing Temporal Sympathy does now is nerf those 3 spells for Mages who don't have Time 2 yet. I would much rather they just made the Temporal Sympathy effects a normal part of the spells (or at least the Time \u2022\u2022+ spells) and given Time a different Lesser Utility Attainment that actually does something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T07:41:23-07:00","id":936538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936522#post936522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still bummed by no more Free Reaches in Legacies Attainments... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in regards to Reach for attainments was changed from the spoilers to the advance pdf or errata. So what are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T07:52:25-07:00","id":936542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936538#post936538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in regards to Reach for attainments was changed from the spoilers to the advance pdf or errata. So what are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd doesn't think Legacy Attainments are powerful enough if they can't reproduce the effects of spells of the same dot level as the Attainment <i>and</i> spend a few Reach on them. There's a whole thread about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T08:04:52-07:00","id":936545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936542#post936542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd doesn't think Legacy Attainments are powerful enough if they can't reproduce the effects of spells of the same dot level as the Attainment <i>and</i> spend a few Reach on them. There's a whole thread about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But he used the words, &quot;no more&quot; indicating there was a change that didn't, in fact, occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T08:13:18-07:00","id":936547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936545#post936545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. But he used the words, &amp;quot;no more&amp;quot; indicating there was a change that didn't, in fact, occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took that to mean &quot;no more free reach than we already had&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:06:34-07:00","id":936711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936470#post936470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean that you can't gank someone and just direct damage him to hell in one turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>that makes me sad, i like dark alleys &amp; fireballs kind of playing on mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936534#post936534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't. I get why the change was made, Temporal Sympathy would have been kind of bonkers if it could send any spell back in time. But with the errata it's practically useless. There are all of three spells that can be affected by Temporal Sympathy that will ever actually be cast without it: Momentary Flux, Postcognition, and Warp. Every other spell that is affected by Temporal Sympathy is a Time spell at 2 dots or higher, so there will never be a time when you can cast such a spell and can't use Temporal Sympathy with it. With this change, lirerally the only thing Temporal Sympathy does now is nerf those 3 spells for Mages who don't have Time 2 yet. I would much rather they just made the Temporal Sympathy effects a normal part of the spells (or at least the Time \u2022\u2022+ spells) and given Time a different Lesser Utility Attainment that actually does something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i think the trade off was worth it. Time 2 attainment was such a mess of implication that the only 2 flimsy limitations stop players to break the game in half with. Either another time mage casting counter spell 24/7 or an oberoni fallacy &quot;changing the timeline willy nilly isnt problematic because the DM can always pull diabolous ex machina to counter them&quot;<br /> <br /> Even though they were joking one of my players nailed it with saying the time 2 attaiments solution of DM`s diabolous ex machina looked like this<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rEdehNpiaEs\" data-code=\"rEdehNpiaEs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rEdehNpiaEs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> However i agree with Charlaquin, they could just remove the attainment and replace it with a lesser utillity one, something along the lines of the highly situational forces one that lets you ignore armor from stationary objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:15:15-07:00","id":936773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936711#post936711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i think the trade off was worth it. Time 2 attainment was such a mess of implication that the only 2 flimsy limitations stop players to break the game in half with. Either another time mage casting counter spell 24/7 or an oberoni fallacy &quot;changing the timeline willy nilly isnt problematic because the DM can always pull diabolous ex machina to counter them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I personally don't share the same concerns about pre-errata Temporal Sympathy, like I said, I can certainly understand why the change was necessary. That kind of play is not for every troupe, and could have put off enough players and especially STs that it is probably healthier for the game to have changed it. It's just that the post-errata Temporal Sympathy Attainment is now literally just a speedbump instead of an actual utility power that bugs me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936711#post936711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However i agree with Charlaquin, they could just remove the attainment and replace it with a lesser utillity one, something along the lines of the highly situational forces one that lets you ignore armor from stationary objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. I'm fine with losing Temporal Sympathy as it used to work, but wish it had been replaced by something useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:26:58-07:00","id":936816,"title":"","content":"I actually highly dislike Forces one, because almost anytime where you can spend a turn doing nothing in order to make your next action better, doing two different actions would end up delivering more presence, especially with how rocket tag-high noon spellslinger mage conflicts tend to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:03:20-07:00","id":936909,"title":"","content":"I very much dislike that the errata mostly made Mind MORE powerful by lowering some of its already strong effects to lower dots, and otherwise making things more potent. Was anyone at all here complaining that Mind wasn't potent enough or something? (Sure, they did make it clear Psychic Domination needs to be active to the conclusion of the task, but that was already implied)<br /> <br /> That said, I like most of the other errata overall, including the Death/Spirit armor changes. I'm flat out ecstatic that Proximi get a single Reach for free now, I always thought it was ridiculous that they always had at least a 1 in 10 or more commonly 3 in 10 chance of losing any blessing they cast instantly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:21:27-07:00","id":936913,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or is Death Armor entirely decoupled from your Death dots now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:58:41-07:00","id":936926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936913#post936913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or is Death Armor entirely decoupled from your Death dots now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Looks like it. It's definitely an improvement, but I'd prefer if there were some other aspect that did depend on Death dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:54:16-07:00","id":936945,"title":"","content":"Conversely, I would have liked the rest of the Mage Armors to have been decoupled from Arcana dots as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T23:00:12-07:00","id":936949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936913#post936913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or is Death Armor entirely decoupled from your Death dots now?</div> </div> </div> </div>And Spirit as well, I think.<br /> <br /> Which at least makes it less of an anomaly, but the inconsistency is still a bit jarring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T23:35:34-07:00","id":936959,"title":"","content":"I think they should have made it so that the Death dots of lethal damage before you need to make rolls stayed in place, but the damage downgrade decoupled like it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T00:16:45-07:00","id":936966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=936945#post936945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, I would have liked the rest of the Mage Armors to have been decoupled from Arcana dots as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works too. I prefer consistency more than anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T17:24:51-07:00","id":937838,"title":"","content":"Better than nothing is my opinion about the errata.<br /> <br /> Eidolon spell was redone and looks okay now (Dave removed the &quot;Nimbus control&quot; b*****t, thank god !), but someone can explain to me why Eidolon isnt Patterning ? In essence its only a &quot;Shape Mana&quot; spell, plus if Eidolon is making then dont make sense that Platonic Form isnt making too, no ?<br /> <br /> Making is completely wrong to me, it looks like more a game balance choice to put one usefull spell to Prime 5 because all the other Prime 5 spells are bad or so, so. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T18:55:21-07:00","id":937865,"title":"","content":"It's Making because you are making life (For loose definition of life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T20:10:54-07:00","id":937899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=937865#post937865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Making because you are making life (For loose definition of life).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, but this dont make any sense.<br /> <br /> 1st, because the <b>Eidolom works the same way as the Golem spells</b> and the two are more &quot;constructs&quot; of &quot;magical machines&quot; than life beings I think. In other words, Eidolom is Golem of Mana/Tass, I think that we can agree about that.<br /> <br /> 2nd, because <b>live beings have at least instincts (see the Create Life spell)</b>, but Golem and Eidolom works only with commands of the creator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The created being is mindless without the conjunctional use of the Mind Arcanum to give it intelligence, <b>acting purely upon instinct</b>. </div> </div> </div><b>They dont interpret, only have pre-programmed action/reactions </b>(maybe a funny example is a &quot;kill my enemy command and Eidlom killing all moving things in the place, even a mouse or the mage waifu&quot;). Plus, the fact of the two not receiving Defense is a evidence of this. And if the creator dont give orders to a Eidolom it will be only a statue.<br /> <br /> 3rd, if Eidolom is a &quot;create life&quot; them the Golem is the same, but the <b>Golem is a Patterning spell</b>. Everything that we say about golem apply to Eidolom and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> 4th, Dave added a effect to the eidolom spell that generates environmental hazards, again this contradict the generate life theory.<br /> <br /> Now talking about the errata,<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sad about no changes with the Balasphemy spell... c'mon that 2 reach dont make any sense.<br /> <br /> A lasting effect that isnt lasting, whats the logic ? The mage can simple make Blasphemy a indefinite duration spell, then why the lasting effect (it says that the effect will be &quot;dispelled by mother nature&quot;, lol) ?<br /> <br /> Plus, in first edition we have a Dead Zone spell that only make sense in &quot;<i>Mind's Eye Theatre: The Awakening</i>&quot; (it gives a penalty to all spells in the dead zone, if I remenber) or combined with that Banisher spell Scorched Earth (again, gives some penalties to spell casting), but the Blasphemy does nothing relevant only tries to mimic a Souless effect that dont make much sense to me.<br /> <br /> Well, at least they will remove the lasting Reach from Eidolom and Platonic form.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last but not least, I'm the only one to think that the Psychic domination need increase the 2 reach effect ? It's soo powerfull for a 2 dot spell and a good number of mages can cast it getting only 2 dice of paradox... Problably the most broken spell to me, I would rule it as a 5 reach effect. This way, the victim have some turns to attack and the caster will need a good number of mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","user":"Sp4rt01","date":". 07-26-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:06:07-07:00","id":937968,"title":"","content":"My group as a whole is pretty immensely disappointed in the gutting of Time, but we'll just houserule the attainment, and Temporal Summoning, to work the way they did before. <br /> <br /> The Fate changes are good, and probably needed.<br /> <br /> The Practice + Primary Factor changes are all excellent. Clarifications on combined spells, also excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:38:19-07:00","id":938068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=937968#post937968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group as a whole is pretty immensely disappointed in the gutting of Time, but we'll just houserule the attainment, and Temporal Summoning, to work the way they did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity: How do you handle &quot;Temporal Sympathy&quot; in your group? I didn't really read to much into time and thought it would work the other way around, that you can use a past image of a subject to cast on the present subject. Like Sympathetic casting, if you see somebody via Postcognition, you can put a Tracker on him via Temporal Sympathy and you would have that tracker on the present subject. Anyway I read it again and realized it works exactly the other way around.<br /> <br /> So how do you handle it if e.g. 3 turns into combat somebody casts honing the form on a character to bolster his past self with +3 strength. Do you roll all the combat rolls again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:00:21-07:00","id":938082,"title":"","content":"We'll according to the errata you can't cast that spell back in time anyway without piggybacking it on a spell that uses Temporal Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:21:03-07:00","id":938093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938082#post938082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll according to the errata you can't cast that spell back in time anyway without piggybacking it on a spell that uses Temporal Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that. But I would like to know how people handle the pre-errata version. Because I have no idea how I would do that.<br /> I also agree that the post-errata version is kind of useless, since it doesn't really add anything. It's more like: &quot;with time 2 you get an attainment, which let's you cast certain time 2 and above spells&quot;. That's kind of redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:12:31-07:00","id":938119,"title":"","content":"If you really wanted a spell casted back in time. Shifting sands time travel and cast it. It's actually fine, the errate just added an extra step, a limiter, and barrier for newbie mages to cross. Combined ShiftingSands+spell you want. This move creates less of a headache. no more throwing spells hundreds of years into the past. no more Killing your rival before they're born nonsense. At two you get basic pre/post-con, and three is the real fireworks show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:22:25-07:00","id":938125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938093#post938093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware of that. But I would like to know how people handle the pre-errata version. Because I have no idea how I would do that.<br /> I also agree that the post-errata version is kind of useless, since it doesn't really add anything. It's more like: &quot;with time 2 you get an attainment, which let's you cast certain time 2 and above spells&quot;. That's kind of redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best suggestion I've seen that I can remember for dealing with spells cast into the past like that is from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> she suggested treating it as a narrative effect spell where the ST decides the logical outcomes and moves the game on. There's no need to go back and play old scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:53:38-07:00","id":938151,"title":"","content":"I have a question about spell stacking and attainments that I didn't see in the errata. Legacy attainments have a rule for stacking with a spell, but I didn't see how normal attainments work with them. Specifically, matter armor and the spell Aegis is what I'm looking at. Both increase your armor (matter armor directly, aegis by reinforcing your gear). Would those stack, or would spell stacking say only the highest effect applies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:08:32-07:00","id":938161,"title":"","content":"Armour produced by Aegis counts as normal armour, I would imagine. If Mage Armour stacks with normal armour, it stacks with Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:17:09-07:00","id":938187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938068#post938068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't really read to much into time and thought it would work the other way around, that you can use a past image of a subject to cast on the present subject. Like Sympathetic casting, if you see somebody via Postcognition, you can put a Tracker on him via Temporal Sympathy and you would have that tracker on the present subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah... That's a really cool idea! What if you could also use things like representations of the subject's past self (a photograph, for instance) as sympathetic Yantras to cast spells on their present self?<br /> <br /> I might rule it to work this way if I run Mage, cause that's really neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:33:13-07:00","id":938192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938068#post938068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do you handle it if e.g. 3 turns into combat somebody casts honing the form on a character to bolster his past self with +3 strength. Do you roll all the combat rolls again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat in our Mage games is extremely rare, and has only lasted longer than a single turn once ever. If that came up (it hasn't), the ST would handle it narratively. We don't reroll dice unless the scene itself gets rewound in its entirety. Generally speaking, for that kind of thing (seeking an advantage in an earlier situation) we just go with Shifting Sands.<br /> <br /> In our group, Temporal Sympathy is mostly used for advancing the narrative, working around obstacles creatively, information gathering, etc. It enables a lot of really fun developments that are impossible without it. <br /> <br /> At the climax of our last story arc, we saved the life of an NPC that was important to one of our allies by using a teamwork, ritually cast Temporal Stutter to throw them into the present from moments before they died - which was years ago. Cue trying to actually explain to the person we just saved what the hell just happened.<br /> <br /> Like Charlaquin, I suppose I understand why it was changed, as I guess it would be problematic for other groups, but it was really, really amazing as-written for ours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:36:19-07:00","id":938196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938119#post938119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really wanted a spell casted back in time. Shifting sands time travel and cast it. It's actually fine, the errate just added an extra step, a limiter, and barrier for newbie mages to cross. Combined ShiftingSands+spell you want. This move creates less of a headache. no more throwing spells hundreds of years into the past. no more Killing your rival before they're born nonsense. At two you get basic pre/post-con, and three is the real fireworks show.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with the erattaed version isn't that you can no longer cast spells back in time. The problem is, all it does now is allow you to cast Momentary Flux on subjects in the past, cast Postcognition on subjects with weaker than Unchanged Temporal Sympathy, and Web-Weaver to bolster Sympathetic Links to things the subject has touched more than one turn ago.<br /> <br /> Every other spell that Temporal Sympathy can explicitly affect is a Time \u2022\u2022 or higher spell, so there will never be a time when you are able to cast them and not be able to use Temporal Sympathy. There would functionally be no difference at all if they didn't require Temporal Sympathy and just made the additions a normal part of those spells. It'd shave a few words off the wordcount too, which is a bonus. Web-Weaver could still have that &quot;Add Time \u2022\u2022&quot; effect even if Time's Lesser Utility Attainment was something else, and again there would be no functional change to the spell. So in effect, the only thing post-errata Temporal Sympathy actually does is locks some of the functionality of Momentary Flux and Postcognition behind a paywall of &quot;buy Time \u2022\u2022 if you want the full effect.&quot; Honestly, I'd be fine with them just bumping those two spells up to Apprentice level if it meant having a Lesser Utility Attainment that actually did something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-27-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:50:17-07:00","id":938206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938196#post938196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every other spell that Temporal Sympathy can explicitly affect is a Time \u2022\u2022 or higher spell, so there will never be a time when you are able to cast them and not be able to use Temporal Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wish people would stop disregarding what using either Sympathy Attainment actually requires, because it's one of those things that screams &quot;this is going to become a popular misconception that leads to nonsensical readings of the setting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:14:44-07:00","id":938220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938206#post938206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish people would stop disregarding what using either Sympathy Attainment actually requires, because it's one of those things that screams &amp;quot;this is going to become a popular misconception that leads to nonsensical readings of the setting.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. It wasn't clear to me that the effects that said &quot;With Temporal Sympathy...&quot; required a sympathetic Yantra, sensory range, and a point of Mana. A lot of them already affect a subject's past without Temporal Sympathy, they just can't go back very far, so I assumed the Attainment merely allowed you to use those spells on targets with weaker Temporal Sympathy and that the other requirements were for when you cast spells into the past that couldn't normally affect the past. Hopefully the errata goes a long way towards making its function clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:18:31-07:00","id":938265,"title":"","content":"I read it as Satchel, but it sounds like some emphasis on the point might be in order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:59:03-07:00","id":938286,"title":"","content":"I haven't absorbed the new time rules, but anything that stops me from having to consider how every other Acanthus in the city (and probably every Cabal in it) will react to current actions in future by casting spells into past makes me happier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:27:47-07:00","id":938380,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I do hear what you're saying, about its functionality utilization. A similar mechanic to temporal sympathy is Sympathetic Range. So I can understand how it can feel underwhelming. Where Sympathetic Range has a really clear identifiable application(distance and interpersonal connections).<br /> <br /> I disagree about regarding word count. TS is simply shorthand for a mechanic that a number of time spells use. Explaining it once and simply referencing it in spell listing is good short hand. Not having it would require the explanation every time you wanted to invoke that mechanic or refer to a previous spells explanation. But indeed more examples and clarification can be helpful.<br /> <br /> I remember playing a TechnoSeer(Space/Time) who used AutoCAD to recreate major events, but I always made it a sticking point that I had to grab reference material. The clues/ site 0 martial I got the better simulation I could get. And this mechanic justifies that playstyle so I am be a little bias. I liked playing that character because he would bootup his computer in the morning and check out his Personal ForeCast. &quot;hummm appears Charlie will bum lunch off of me again, take the side exit 11:58&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:54:26-07:00","id":938406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938265#post938265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it as Satchel, but it sounds like some emphasis on the point might be in order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Satchel's interpretation is correct. Mine was a misunderstanding based on an assumption of how the Attainment worked pre-errata. I still believe the post-errata version would be better off incorporated into the spells themselves, and Time given a Lesser Utility Attainment that isn't all-drawback, but I was mistaken in believing it would be functionally the same as it is now, at least not without adding a lot of extra wordcount. And I appreciate <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> correcting me on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938286#post938286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't absorbed the new time rules, but anything that stops me from having to consider how every other Acanthus in the city (and probably every Cabal in it) will react to current actions in future by casting spells into past makes me happier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. I don't disagree. I just want Time's Lesser Utility Attainment to be replaced with something useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938380#post938380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I do hear what you're saying, about its functionality utilization. A similar mechanic to temporal sympathy is Sympathetic Range. So I can understand how it can feel underwhelming. Where Sympathetic Range has a really clear identifiable application(distance and interpersonal connections).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic Range is a good comparison, because it has its own use, independent of specific Space spells. Temporal Sympathy, under the errata, does not. It allows some specific Time spells to do more, at the cost of a point of Mana, a sympathetic Yantra, and sensory range. To me, that feels less like a utility power and more like a pay gate you have to get through to access some of your spells' full functionality. I'm ok with those things being required to expand those spells functionality. But I would also like Time to get a Lesser Utility Attainment that did something independent of specific Time spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938380#post938380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree about regarding word count. TS is simply shorthand for a mechanic that a number of time spells use. Explaining it once and simply referencing it in spell listing is good short hand. Not having it would require the explanation every time you wanted to invoke that mechanic or refer to a previous spells explanation. But indeed more examples and clarification can be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as per above, that was a mistake based on my misreading of how TS worked pre-errata.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:18:51-07:00","id":938500,"title":"","content":"To be fair, like almost all of the lesser utility are pretty &quot;ueseless&quot; - The Eye of series can be made irrelevant with one dot spells (this makes them mostly a luxury ability), Forces is...extremely specific and requires pretty harsh requirements that make it somewhat useless for situations where it could be useful, Matter is semi-useful but only when casting Matter spells pretty much, Life would be OK if it didn't require Instant Action activation (and if Knit wasn't errated to healing Lethal for reach)...Fate is the only outright amazing (probably too amazing) choice, because it gives you spell factors for mana, and is veeeeeeeeeeeery easy to use.<br /> <br /> Remember that you can also Combine Time Spells with other spells, and the whole Combination can benefit from Temporal Sympathy. I suspect a lot of what you want might be hidden in this feature.<br /> ...we have two Time 2 players, I'm sick and we have a game this sunday. Could someone write a step-by-step &quot;guide to Temporal Sympathy&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-27-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:38:34-07:00","id":938554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938406#post938406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathetic Range is a good comparison, because it has its own use, independent of specific Space spells. Temporal Sympathy, under the errata, does not. It allows some specific Time spells to do more, at the cost of a point of Mana, a sympathetic Yantra, and sensory range. To me, that feels less like a utility power and more like a pay gate you have to get through to access some of your spells' full functionality. I'm ok with those things being required to expand those spells functionality. But I would also like Time to get a Lesser Utility Attainment that did something independent of specific Time spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, as per above, that was a mistake based on my misreading of how TS worked pre-errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sympathetic Range also has a cost of a mana and a yant to use it. They're symmetrical. Space is a measure of &quot;Correspondence&quot; between two entities. Time is the measure of &quot;Correspondence&quot; between to periods. Re-Reading a few time spells, I can see your view point. But I can tell you as long has the effect that you want is only a minor difference from the current Unchanged Present, you may not even need temporal sympathy.<br /> <br /> And yes I can see where Sympathetic Range is called for in spells outside Space's Spell list(Timenoless). While TS is called almost exculisivly within the Time list. These were used when the location of the target was in question. I can only guess you would bring up temporal sympathy when the Time of the Target is in question? But I will say combining spell is art meant to bridge what isn't in the system. so I do see this restriction of needing to combind the spells to be annoying, it still falls into the system framework they're trying to use so I'm ok with it. Having the option to go beyond your gnoise softcap still makes me giddy. Expertise with limited power<br /> <br /> Temporal Summoning page 189-190.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without the Temporal<br /> Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to<br /> the present, but this is still sufficient to remove most Conditions<br /> and heal injuries. By employing Temporal Sympathy, the mage<br /> can restore ancient ruins to their inhabited state, return her enemies<br /> to childhood, or even bring the dead back to life. When<br /> the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject immediately returns to its<br /> present self. </div> </div> </div>I would consider restoring an old ruin to be a more momumental task then pushing back wounds. Thus if we were using the reach mechainic I would say the difference required more reach. and the temporal sympathy range charts/mechianic help visualize that.<br /> <br /> To the second point: Ah my fault for not reading that post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:40:24-07:00","id":938585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938554#post938554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sympathetic Range also has a cost of a mana and a yant to use it. They're symmetrical. Space is a measure of &quot;Correspondence&quot; between two entities. Time is the measure of &quot;Correspondence&quot; between to periods. Re-Reading a few time spells, I can see your view point. But I can tell you as long has the effect that you want is only a minor difference from the current Unchanged Present, you may not even need temporal sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're designed to be symmetrical, but Sympathetic Range can be used with any spell, whereas Temporal Sympathy can (now) only be used with specific spells. They have the same cost but vastly different utility. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938554#post938554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes I can see where Sympathetic Range is called for in spells outside Space's Spell list(Timenoless). While TS is called almost exculisivly within the Time list. These were used when the location of the target was in question. I can only guess you would bring up temporal sympathy when the Time of the Target is in question? But I will say combining spell is art meant to bridge what isn't in the system. so I do see this restriction of needing to combind the spells to be annoying, it still falls into the system framework they're trying to use so I'm ok with it. Having the option to go beyond your gnoise softcap still makes me giddy. Expertise with limited power</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is Sympathetic Range called for outside of the Space spell list, it can be used on any spell, even if it's not specifically called for. And the need to use combined spells to affect things in the past with non-Time spells isn't what bothers me. I've said all along I understand why that decision was made. I'm cool with that. What I'm not cool with is Time's Lesser Utility Attainment being useless outside of a few specific spells. Just bake that effect into the spells (including the Mana cost and the requirement of sensory range and a sympathetic Yantra if need be) and give Time a Lesser Utility Attainment that actually has utility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938554#post938554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporal Summoning page 189-190.<br /> <br /> I would consider restoring an old ruin to be a more momumental task then pushing back wounds. Thus if we were using the reach mechainic I would say the difference required more reach. and the temporal sympathy range charts/mechianic help visualize that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get that, it's fine to have additional requirements to affect things further back in time, and the Temporal Sympathy chart is a useful tool for doing that. Just don't waste Time's Lesser Utility Attainment on that mechanic if you're only going to use it for 6 spells and say it can't be used for anything else.<br /> <br /> Forget the comparison to Sympathetic Range, <i>no</i> Arcanum has a Lesser Utility Attainment that does literally nothing but limit the power of 5 of that Arcanum's spells and 1 other spell if you don't use it. With this errata, Temporal Sympathy isn't a utility power, it's a tax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:46:09-07:00","id":938588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938585#post938585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget the comparison to Sympathetic Range, <i>no</i> Arcanum has a Lesser Utility Attainment that does literally nothing but limit the power of 5 of that Arcanum's spells and 1 other spell if you don't use it. With this errata, Temporal Sympathy isn't a utility power, it's a tax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't talk as though a non-spell thing that you can do with your magic by virtue of having a certain number of dots in the Arcanum is an air-breathing mermaid power that doesn't warrant an Attainment slot just because a hole was plugged that didn't exist for the concept in 1e.<br /> <br /> You can time-travel more than a few seconds prior to archmastery in 2e. That doesn't warrant turning Temporal Sympathy into the Slipshanking Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:51:34-07:00","id":938590,"title":"","content":"Well, my own thought so far is a simple HR, to adapt it to the needs of my group.<br /> <br /> Temporal Sympathy can still cast spells back (or forward) in time but it can NOT change the past, only those particular spells (Shifting Sands etc) can do that. The main benefits of it would be that unless the spell lasts all the time up until the present... no spell control required. Casting it into the future? Sure, it'll count against spell control... at that point, not before.<br /> <br /> In essence you can gather information from the past, even using other arcana, or other things that won't actually change the timeline noticeably (and yes, this is subjective, that's what you have a Devil/GM for) and you can cast spells forward in time without having to actually have spell control wasted while you're waiting for them, and you also save on duration factors since it's duration starts from that point.<br /> <br /> I, personally, think that this might work for out group but I will be honest, I'm still wary of the fact that I might have a blindspot so... if you see something broken in it tell me now please? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:00:55-07:00","id":938594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938500#post938500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, like almost all of the lesser utility are pretty &quot;ueseless&quot; - The Eye of series can be made irrelevant with one dot spells (this makes them mostly a luxury ability), Forces is...extremely specific and requires pretty harsh requirements that make it somewhat useless for situations where it could be useful, Matter is semi-useful but only when casting Matter spells pretty much, Life would be OK if it didn't require Instant Action activation (and if Knit wasn't errated to healing Lethal for reach)...Fate is the only outright amazing (probably too amazing) choice, because it gives you spell factors for mana, and is veeeeeeeeeeeery easy to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're as their names imply, lesser utility powers. Useful in specific situations or broadly applicable but not especially powerful. Conditional Duration, Universal Counterspell, and Sympathetic Range are all far more powerful than the others, and until the errata, so was Temporal Sympathy, so like I've said, I'm cool with it getting nerfed. But what bothers me is limiting it to six specific spells. I would rather those spells just be able to do the thing (for the extra cost), and Time get a Lesser Utility Attainment like Eyes of Whatever that did something besides being a mana and reach tax.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938500#post938500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that you can also Combine Time Spells with other spells, and the whole Combination can benefit from Temporal Sympathy. I suspect a lot of what you want might be hidden in this feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember. Changing Time's Lesser Utility Attainment wouldn't remove the ability to do that. I am fine with the changes to the way Temporal Sympathy works, what I object to is Temporal Sympathy taking up Time's Lesser Utility Attainment slot when it has no utility and in fact limits the utility of the spells that require it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938500#post938500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...we have two Time 2 players, I'm sick and we have a game this sunday. Could someone write a step-by-step &quot;guide to Temporal Sympathy&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote myself from another thread,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912850-how-does-temporal-sympathy-attainment-works?p=914459#post914459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Temporal Sympathy chart works just like the Sympathetic Range chart, only instead of casting across distance and the strength of the connection being determined by how closely associated the subjects are with each other, Temporal Sympathy casts across time and the strength of the connection is determined by how different the subject's present self is from the version of the subject you are casting on in the past. Often, the more time has passed, the more the subject will have changed. For example, a 50 year old man probably has a Medium connection to his 5-year-old self, maybe even a Weak connection. On the other hand, a 500 year old rock might have an Unchanged connection with its 50 year old self if it has remained relatively untouched in that time. Conversely, if that rock gets carved into a sculpture tomorrow, that sculpture will probably only have a Weak connection with the rock it was carved from, even though it just happened a day ago.<br /> <br /> The numbers in the far right column are used as the Withstand when you are casting a spell on a past version of something. For example, if you tripped and broke your arm, and wanted to cast Exceptional Luck on yourself before you broke your arm to hopefully prevent that from happening, the connection would probably be Strong, giving your past self a Withstand of 1 against the spell. Unless you waited until after the injury had time to heal up a bit, in which case you would probably have a Medium connection to yourself before the injury, and the Withstand would be 2. The numbers in the second column from the left are used as the Withstand when you are casting a spell on the Temporal Sympathetic connection between two subjects. For example, if you wanted to make everyone forget the historic significance of the a landmark, you could cast a spell to weaken or destroy its Temporal Sympathy with itself from before it was considered significant. For example, the Liberty Bell probably has Medium sympathy with itself before it was cracked, so that connection would have a Withstand of 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that post was written before the errata, so now you would need to also combine the spell you wanted to cast on the past with an appropriate Time spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:05:07-07:00","id":938596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938588#post938588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't talk as though a non-spell thing that you can do with your magic by virtue of having a certain number of dots in the Arcanum is an air-breathing mermaid power that doesn't warrant an Attainment slot just because a hole was plugged that didn't exist for the concept in 1e.<br /> <br /> You can time-travel more than a few seconds prior to archmastery in 2e. That doesn't warrant turning Temporal Sympathy into the Slipshanking Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the zillionth time, I'm cool with Temporal Sympathy only working on specific spells. I'm not cool with Time's Lesser Utility Attainment only working on specific spells. I would rather have those spells be modified so that Temporal Sympathy isn't required, or is a part of the spell itself, and Time have something other than Temporal Sympathy as its Lesser Utility Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:37:16-07:00","id":938613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938596#post938596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the zillionth time, I'm cool with Temporal Sympathy only working on specific spells. I'm not cool with Time's Lesser Utility Attainment only working on specific spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've repeatedly undersold &quot;Time spells that call for Temporal Sympathy&quot; as &quot;printed Time spells that specifically mention temporal sympathy&quot; rather than &quot;Time spells whose effects could logically have their scope expanded through the use of temporal sympathy, or replicate Space spells dealing with sympathy as alluded to in the topic's description.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Spells that could logically have their scope expanded through the use of temporal sympathy&quot; includes most time-travel spells and postcognitive affairs and anything in the same neck of the woods, which still have notable applications even in the near-immediate term and comprise half of the Arcanum's purview besides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would rather have those spells be modified so that Temporal Sympathy isn't required, or is a part of the spell itself, and Time have something other than Temporal Sympathy as its Lesser Utility Attainment. </div> </div> </div>You're saying you would rather an Attainment <i>not be an Attainment</i>, which is the point of my contention. It's an Arcanum-based ability that influences how some of your spells work. <i>That is what an Attainment is</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:48:38-07:00","id":938614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938613#post938613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've repeatedly undersold &quot;Time spells that call for Temporal Sympathy&quot; as &quot;printed Time spells that specifically mention temporal sympathy&quot; rather than &quot;Time spells whose effects could logically have their scope expanded through the use of temporal sympathy, or replicate Space spells dealing with sympathy as alluded to in the topic's description.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Spells that could logically have their scope expanded through the use of temporal sympathy&quot; includes most time-travel spells and postcognitive affairs and anything in the same neck of the woods, which still have notable applications even in the near-immediate term and comprise half of the Arcanum's purview besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose. I mostly don't have very a good sense of when to allow Temporal Sympathy to affect a creatively cast spell and when not to when it's only supposed to affect spells that specifically call for it. I don't see the through line between the printed spells that do call for it, making it difficult for me to judge when to allow it and when not to on creative spells. I suppose that's my own failing, but as someone who doesn't totally grokk creative thaumaturgy quite yet, I would prefer the Attainments all be useful in games where only the printed spells are used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938613#post938613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're saying you would rather an Attainment <i>not be an Attainment</i>, which is the point of my contention. It's an Arcanum-baed ability that influences how some of your spells work. <i>That is what an Attainment is</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am saying I would rather it not be an attainment. Because I don't think its utility justifies it being so. It could just as easily be done through a few Reach, Mana, and/or &quot;Add Time X&quot; effects tacked on to the small number of printed spells it affects, and in my opinion that makes it lackluster as an Attainment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should also point out that I'm not expecting, or even asking for Temporal Sympathy or the Time 2 Attainment to actually be changed. I'm just expressing my disappointment with the errata. I've actually already decided how I plan to house rule it if I run Mage, based on someone's earlier suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-28-2016, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:49:52-07:00","id":938615,"title":"","content":"No, an Attainment is an ability developed by understanding your Arcanum, reflected by gaining a new, small power. Only a small subset of these powers deals with modding some of your spells. Saying that you would prefer this Attainment to be other kind of Attainment doesn't mean that you trying to make it a non-Attainment. Mage Armors aren't modyfing how your spells works, and they are Attainments. Mage Sight modifiers don't modify your spells, yet they are Attainments. &quot;Protect me From Z&quot; abilities of Fate and Death do not modify your spells, yet they are Attainments.<br /> The critique here is that Temporal Sympathy is a prereq for spells, not a new ability, which - at this point - could be just backed into these spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:12:40-07:00","id":938629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938615#post938615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, an Attainment is an ability developed by understanding your Arcanum, reflected by gaining a new, small power. Only a small subset of these powers deals with modding some of your spells. Saying that you would prefer this Attainment to be other kind of Attainment doesn't mean that you trying to make it a non-Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantics games aside, no, &quot;make the Lesser Utility Attainment for the Time Arcanum something other than Temporal Sympathy and relegate the effects of the Temporal Sympathy Attainment to a byline in a few printed spells that otherwise duplicates the costs attached to the Sympathetic Range Attainment&quot; is precisely &quot;making Temporal Sympathy a non-Attainment,&quot; unless you think I'm claiming that any replacement for Temporal Sympathy is not an Attainment, which would be nonsensical to the point of absurdity.<br /> <br /> Temporal Sympathy is only a &quot;tax&quot; or &quot;required&quot; if your assumption is the spells that can use it have no use without it, which is entirely circular reasoning and not borne out by any of the specific examples available, all of which go into a fair amount of detail about what they can do with an Unchanged sympathetic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2016, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:35:12-07:00","id":938639,"title":"","content":"Why wasn't Sympathetic Range changed in the same way that Temporal Sympathy was?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the answer is that Sympathetic Range wasn't as 'unbalanced'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:46:55-07:00","id":938650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938639#post938639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wasn't Sympathetic Range changed in the same way that Temporal Sympathy was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic Range has always operated as a vector for more spells than the Space Arcanum alone and doesn't open up an entire Ashton Kutcher film's worth of territory whose maps need redrawn when allowed to apply to intermediate forms of influence between scrutiny and wholesale revisitation.<br /> <br /> The strange and distant past being harder to clearly see is a sensible analog to clairvoyance being harder to use on a place you've never even seen; using a voodoo doll to harm someone from three countries away is not on the same level as burning a photograph to retroactively killmurder somebody in terms of Things Any Apprentice Can Do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:52:35-07:00","id":938654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938650#post938650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathetic Range has always operated as a vector for more spells than the Space Arcanum alone and doesn't open up an entire Ashton Kutcher film's worth of territory whose maps need redrawn when allowed to apply to intermediate forms of influence between scrutiny and wholesale revisitation.<br /> <br /> The strange and distant past being harder to clearly see is a sensible analog to clairvoyance being harder to use on a place you've never even seen; using a voodoo doll to harm someone from three countries away is not on the same level as burning a photograph to retroactively killmurder somebody in terms of Things Any Apprentice Can Do.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in addition to not being as unbalanced, the additional reasoning is 'Well, it didn't work that way in 1E'?<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, I'm trying to see if I can see any reason for actually implementing this change in my game. I find arguments for balance un-compelling, and I have no investment in keeping things similar to first edition, so if there are other practical differences between the two attainments that I may not be considering that make changing this a good idea, I'd like to know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-28-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T00:38:41-07:00","id":938673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938654#post938654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in addition to not being as unbalanced, the additional reasoning is 'Well, it didn't work that way in 1E'?<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, I'm trying to see if I can see any reason for actually implementing this change in my game. I find arguments for balance un-compelling, and I have no investment in keeping things similar to first edition, so if there are other practical differences between the two attainments that I may not be considering that make changing this a good idea, I'd like to know</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking into the past or calling its afterimages forward doesn't necessitate any special consideration, redoing turns is comparatively trivial, and redoing scenes or changing common history more drastically is sufficiently risky to constitute the stuff of larger Plot.<br /> <br /> The same cannot be said for a significant portion of starting characters needing ST fiat to stop them from chucking spell effects back in time indefinitely like Steins;Gate with a GameShark. That's not a balance concern so much as making it clear that the mechanics in place around time travel supply a narrative framework that's meant to be engaged rather than ignored with the likes of Fireballs From the Future.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic Range doesn't require the ST to figure out entire domino effects that might change the lives of entire neighborhoods in the time it takes for a PC to prepare and cast a spell; Temporal Sympathy evidently wasn't meant to either, and hoping players will be considerate enough to minimize the impact of changes they aren't even willing to put boots to the pavement for is a bit much to expect for a game that is not AetherCo's Continuum or similar products that specifically revolve around time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T02:43:35-07:00","id":938701,"title":"","content":"After rereading the other attainment I actually completely agree with Satchel. Temporal Sympathy is a lot less broader usable post-errata than it was before, but it is still quite useful and in the line with &quot;Permanance&quot; for example. The fate and space 2 dot attainments can be argued to be the most useful, or at least most broadly applicable, but some of the other attainments are pretty niche, too.<br /> I also agree that the pre errata version is a mess if players start to abuse it. While there certainly may be groups which have no problem using this carefully and mainly narrative, time travell can fuck up a lot of groups and I think it is good that for the time spells that allow it, it is clearly stated how to resolve this. I remember a session in a science fiction game were we got our hands on a warship, which was also a time machine and had just destroyed a planet. We discussed for more than two hours what would actually happen if we travel back in time and destroy the past ship with the present ship before the destruction. Our gamemaster literally started crying!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938654#post938654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in addition to not being as unbalanced, the additional reasoning is 'Well, it didn't work that way in 1E'?<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, I'm trying to see if I can see any reason for actually implementing this change in my game. I find arguments for balance un-compelling, and I have no investment in keeping things similar to first edition, so if there are other practical differences between the two attainments that I may not be considering that make changing this a good idea, I'd like to know</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything you mentioned so far Indov can still be done with the appropriate time spell.<br /> <br /> I would therefore simply argue through simplification. The new temporal sympathy makes it clearer how to influence the past and how to resolve it. Instead of basically be able to use ANY spell via temporal sympathy to influence the past, you now need to use time spells first and foremost. It's kind of what the arcanum is for anyway. Temporal sympathy is now nothing more but rules for how to influence the further past, since this should get more and more difficult.<br /> Additionally to get BETTER at influencing something with weaker temporal sympathy, you actually need to get better in the TIME arcanum, not just any arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 07-28-2016, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:14:21-07:00","id":938772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938701#post938701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporal sympathy is now nothing more but rules for how to influence the further past, since this should get more and more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a perfect summary of my issue with the change. Every other Arcanum gets a two-dot Attainment that is an ability in its own right. Time gets a rule for how to use Time spells that it can't access until Apprentice. It's not a utility power, it's a speed bump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:35:49-07:00","id":938789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938772#post938772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a perfect summary of my issue with the change. Every other Arcanum gets a two-dot Attainment that is an ability in its own right. Time gets a rule for how to use Time spells that it can't access until Apprentice. It's not a utility power, it's a speed bump.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ. The Death, Matter, Mind and Spirit attainments, don't do any more either. Temporal Sympathy let's you influence the further past. So it adds more options to time magic. Death, Mind and Spirit basically only improve your corresponding mage sight and give you the ability to interact with certain phenomena, while the Matter attainmaint does nothing but making it easier to let Matter spells last longer. So the new Temporal Sympathy is totally in line with these.<br /> One could still argue, that fate and space 2 dot attainments are probably a bit stronger than the other ones, but it's not that Time is the only weak one and all the others totally rock.<br /> I actually think it is a good change and since as an Acanthus you are likely to both have Temporal Sympathy and Conditional Duration, you are doing pretty good with attainments.<br /> <br /> I also think that nobody would actually care if the post errata version of Temporal Sympathy would have been in the first version of the book. Everybody would think: &quot;Hey it's great I can influence stuff in the past with this!&quot;, instead of only thinking about how much more you could do with the previous version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:15:36-07:00","id":938815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938789#post938789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beg to differ. The Death, Matter, Mind and Spirit attainments, don't do any more either. Temporal Sympathy let's you influence the further past. So it adds more options to time magic. Death, Mind and Spirit basically only improve your corresponding mage sight and give you the ability to interact with certain phenomena, while the Matter attainmaint does nothing but making it easier to let Matter spells last longer. So the new Temporal Sympathy is totally in line with these.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue has nothing to do with &quot;how much you can do&quot; with the Attainment. My issue is that it's not an ability in its own right. Being able to spend mana instead of Reach on the Duration of your Matter spells may have limited application, but it's an expansion of what the character can do beyond the base spellcasting rules. Being able to see ghosts, spirits, and Goetia with Peripheral Mage Sight may be a minor benefit, but it's an ability that expands what the character is capable of beyond the base Mage Sight rules. Temporal Sympathy is a switch that a handful of spells check to see if you have turned on before you can get part of their effect. No other Arcanum has a Lesser Utility Attainment that relies on specific spells to give it permission to work and to specify what it is allowed to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938789#post938789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could still argue, that fate and space 2 dot attainments are probably a bit stronger than the other ones, but it's not that Time is the only weak one and all the others totally rock.<br /> I actually think it is a good change and since as an Acanthus you are likely to both have Temporal Sympathy and Conditional Duration, you are doing pretty good with attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have zero interest in how &quot;strong&quot; or &quot;weak&quot; the Attainments are. I care about the way they are designed. I want them all to be expansions on the baseline mechanics, not limitations on the baseline mechanics that get removed when you have enough dots. Currently, all of them satisfy that design goal except Temporal Sympathy. I want &quot;with [Time 2 Attainment], you can...&quot; instead of &quot;without [Time 2 Attainment], you can't...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938789#post938789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that nobody would actually care if the post errata version of Temporal Sympathy would have been in the first version of the book. Everybody would think: &quot;Hey it's great I can influence stuff in the past with this!&quot;, instead of only thinking about how much more you could do with the previous version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except no, I would have thought &quot;why is this whole table and set of rules for Temporal Sympathy in here when it only matters for six specific spells that tell you exactly what the Attainment allows them to do different?&quot; and &quot;why does the parallel Sympathy mechanic work with any spell at all without having to be combined with one of a few specific space spells?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:32:42-07:00","id":938831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938815#post938815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except no, I would have thought &quot;why is this whole table and set of rules for Temporal Sympathy in here when it only matters for six specific spells that tell you exactly what the Attainment allows them to do different?&quot; and &quot;why does the parallel Sympathy mechanic work with any spell at all without having to be combined with one of a few specific space spells?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I would suggest, that it does work with creative thaumaturgy and therefore does expand what you can do with time magic quite significantly and not only for the written down spells that call for it. And I think this is important, since it gives rules for interacting with changed subjects and those rules go beyond what regular spell casting can do. No regular spell calls for specific yantras or sympathetic connections and so on. So you do need to rule this stuff somehow to make it applicable for creative thaumaturgy and I think a low level attainment is a quite neat way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:41:21-07:00","id":938835,"title":"","content":"The original Temporal Sympathy also worked with creative thaumauturgy so you cannot claim that the errata version expands anything.<br /> <br /> So far I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> has the more compelling position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:51:24-07:00","id":938846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938831#post938831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I would suggest, that it does work with creative thaumaturgy and therefore does expand what you can do with time magic quite significantly and not only for the written down spells that call for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but when Temporal Sympathy explicitly only works with spells that specifically call for it, it's much harder to figure out when designing a spell whether it should be able to work with Temporal Sympathy or not. Especially when one of the printed spells that works with it isn't even a Time spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938831#post938831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think this is important, since it gives rules for interacting with changed subjects and those rules go beyond what regular spell casting can do. No regular spell calls for specific yantras or sympathetic connections and so on. So you do need to rule this stuff somehow to make it applicable for creative thaumaturgy and I think a low level attainment is a quite neat way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if Temporal Sympathy worked with any Time spell, this would be a much more compelling argument for me. But as it stands, there are specific spells it's allowed to work with and it isn't allowed to work with anything else. Can I just use Creative Thaumaturgy to make a Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell that deals damage to someone in the past? Presumably not, since Rend Lifespan doesn't work with Temporal Sympathy. How about a Space \u2022\u2022\u2022 spell that weakens a Sympathetic Connection in the past? Judging by Web Weaver, apparently that isn't too far out of the realm of possibility. But what about stuff with less obvious points of comparison? What if I want to make like a Death spell that messes with the past version of someone's soul? Is that something I can design in such a way that it specifically calls for Temporal Sympathy, or is that something I would have to combine with Rewrite History or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:05:37-07:00","id":938855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938815#post938815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;why does the parallel Sympathy mechanic work with any spell at all without having to be combined with one of a few specific space spells?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This <i>continues</i> to be a false equivalence that ignores things like &quot;there is no spatial magical equivalent of The Present Moves On et al.&quot; Mage's approach to time is not interchangeable with its approach to space just because both Arcana of the same names use similar mechanics to represent the degree of alignment particular subjects have with particular other subjects.<br /> <br /> The game is set in the present, which does not and cannot move backwards as a result of your stepping into the past through conventional Time spells \u2014 &quot;the present&quot; is not the temporal equivalent of the spatial &quot;here&quot; for the purposes of of Awakened magic that alters it. Overlapping points in time is a lot less ambiguously time travel than colocation is ambiguously teleportation on the basis of consequences alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938846#post938846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if Temporal Sympathy worked with any Time spell, this would be a much more compelling argument for me. But as it stands, there are specific spells it's allowed to work with and it isn't allowed to work with anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the word &quot;specific&quot; appears nowhere in the relevant text.<br /> <br /> I struggle to see how &quot;if a spell's effect would logically cause the ripples that register to Active Time Sight, it requires actual time travel&quot; is difficult to figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:22:00-07:00","id":938862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938835#post938835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Temporal Sympathy also worked with creative thaumauturgy so you cannot claim that the errata version expands anything.<br /> <br /> So far I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> has the more compelling position.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument never was, that the new Temporal Sympathy can do MORE than the old one, quite the opposite. My argument to put it very simple is: you NEED rules for Temporal Sympathy and an attainment makes the most sense. Why not keeping the old one then? Because it is breaking the system.<br /> <br /> So while this might not be very compelling, it's the only logical way I can see to make Temporal Sympathy work somehow. And if you don't care about &quot;weak&quot; or &quot;strong&quot; or &quot;broadly&quot; or &quot;narrowly applicable&quot; stop comparing it with Sympathetic Range. Sympathetic Range is not breaking the system.<br /> <br /> Temporal Sympathy is something you need for certain time spells. The mechanic is the same for all these spells and could be used for creative thaumaturgy as well. Since it is the same mechanic you add to different spells and this mechanic is deeply assciated with Time magic, it makes sense to make an attainment out of it. It was narrowed in it's use with the errata because the developers saw a need for this systemwise.<br /> <br /> So if your group is fine with the old one, just keep it. But I really don't see any other way to have Temporal Sympathy in the system at all if not as an attainment, even if the use is relatively narrow.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938855#post938855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the word &quot;specific&quot; appears nowhere in the relevant text.<br /> <br /> I struggle to see how &quot;if a spell's effect would logically cause the ripples that register to Active Time Sight, it requires actual time travel&quot; is difficult to figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the errate does say:<br /> &quot;Time 2: Temporal Sympathy: Only works on Time spells that call for it, or other spells combined with a suitable Time spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> So there are quite a lot of Time spells which don't call for Temporal Sympathy and therefore don't need it. But I think this is more because you simply don't interact with subjects with other than &quot;unchanged&quot; sympathy in this spells and makes Temporal Sympathy therefore irrelevant. So basically: it works with all Time spells, but most written out Time spells simply don't need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 07-28-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:40:23-07:00","id":938874,"title":"","content":"I think simpler than changing the attainment would have been to say a thing cannot be sent back before it existed in the same way that Corridors of Time does unless the spell specifically screws with the past in the same way that Corridors of Time or Shifting Sands does. So you couldn't send a spell back in time to a point before it existed. This would nix the potential problem of sending Honing the Form or whatever back into the past which has not been solved by the errata despite the fact that the errata seems to have been provided in order to address that very problem.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with you that you need rules for Temporal Sympathy, and I agree with you that an attainment for it makes sense. What I do disagree with is the way you put your argument which is that things are so much clearer now with the errata (They're not, just more restrictive in a way that ultimately doesn't change anything), and that it's all good because Creative Thaumaturgy somehow fixes the increased limitation problem (It doesn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-28-2016, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:41:04-07:00","id":938875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938862#post938862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the errate does say</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about <i>specific</i> spells.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spells <i>that call for it</i>&quot; is a wider net than &quot;'only' a quarter of the printed example spells for the Arcanum and no others.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:31:28-07:00","id":938927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938855#post938855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This <i>continues</i> to be a false equivalence that ignores things like &quot;there is no spatial magical equivalent of The Present Moves On et al.&quot; Mage's approach to time is not interchangeable with its approach to space just because both Arcana of the same names use similar mechanics to represent the degree of alignment particular subjects have with particular other subjects.<br /> <br /> The game is set in the present, which does not and cannot move backwards as a result of your stepping into the past through conventional Time spells \u2014 &quot;the present&quot; is not the temporal equivalent of the spatial &quot;here&quot; for the purposes of of Awakened magic that alters it. Overlapping points in time is a lot less ambiguously time travel than colocation is ambiguously teleportation on the basis of consequences alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read my suggestions for possible house rules, you'll notice that I'm perfectly fine with Temporal Sympathy and Sympathetic Range being asymmetrical. I was merely stating what my initial reaction would have been if the advance PDF had featured the post-errata functionality of Temporal Sympathy from the get-go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938855#post938855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the word &quot;specific&quot; appears nowhere in the relevant text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, are there any spells that <i>nonspecifically</i> call for Temporal Sympathy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938855#post938855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggle to see how &quot;if a spell's effect would logically cause the ripples that register to Active Time Sight, it requires actual time travel&quot; is difficult to figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how Momentary Flux or Postcognition would cause ripples in Time Sight, since they don't change the past in any way, but they can still be cast on subjects in the past with Temporal Sympathy. Casting Rend Lifespan on someone in the past would certainly create ripples, but it isn't able to be cast on a subject in the past with Temporal Sympathy. Rewrite History would certainly create ripples, and it can be used on a subject in the past without Temporal Sympathy as long as the subject has Unchanged Sympathy with its present self, but does require it if the Sympathy is any weaker. Shifting Sands is actual time travel but doesn't require Temporal Sympathy. Corridors of Time is actual time travel that does require Temporal Sympathy if the subject has weaker than Unchanged Temporal Sympathy with itself at the time you send it back to. Web-Weaver isn't even a Time spell but can be used on subjects in the past with Temporal Sympathy and without being combined with a Time spell.<br /> <br /> Maybe the quality of a spell that allows it to qualify for Temporal Sympathy is obvious to you, but you have consistently demonstrated a far better intuitive grasp of rules interactions than the average CofD fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-28-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:49:44-07:00","id":938945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938862#post938862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument never was, that the new Temporal Sympathy can do MORE than the old one, quite the opposite. My argument to put it very simple is: you NEED rules for Temporal Sympathy and an attainment makes the most sense. Why not keeping the old one then? Because it is breaking the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily agree that you need rules for Temporal Sympathy. There are already tools like &quot;+X Reach&quot;, &quot;add [Arcanum] X&quot;, &quot;This effect requires the character to spend X Mana&quot; and combined spells. If affecting the past with is going to be limited to a subset of possible spells anyway, why not use those tools instead of writing a whole subsystem for it and using up one of Time's Attainments on &quot;you are allowed to use this subsystem when a spell calls for it&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938862#post938862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while this might not be very compelling, it's the only logical way I can see to make Temporal Sympathy work somehow. And if you don't care about &amp;quot;weak&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;strong&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;broadly&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;narrowly applicable&amp;quot; stop comparing it with Sympathetic Range. Sympathetic Range is not breaking the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually avoided comparing it to Sympathetic Range until other people started bringing it up. I don't care if Temporal Sympathy looks anything like Sympathetic Range or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938862#post938862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporal Sympathy is something you need for certain time spells. The mechanic is the same for all these spells and could be used for creative thaumaturgy as well. Since it is the same mechanic you add to different spells and this mechanic is deeply assciated with Time magic, it makes sense to make an attainment out of it. It was narrowed in it's use with the errata because the developers saw a need for this systemwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that a separate subsystem is needed to handle these cases if it's only going to be applicable to a limited number of spells. If it was &quot;all Time spells&quot; I would agree with you. If it was &quot;spells of any Arcanum where affecting the past is part of the effect&quot;, it wouldn't be a functional change because there would be nothing stopping you from designing a spell that is identical to a printed spell, except that it works on the subject's past and therefore interacts with Temporal Sympathy. As it is now, I can't really tell what the rules are for what spells can interact with Temporal Sympathy because not all Time spells do and there's one non-Time spell that does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938862#post938862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the errate does say:<br /> &amp;quot;Time 2: Temporal Sympathy: Only works on Time spells that call for it, or other spells combined with a suitable Time spell.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So there are quite a lot of Time spells which don't call for Temporal Sympathy and therefore don't need it. But I think this is more because you simply don't interact with subjects with other than &amp;quot;unchanged&amp;quot; sympathy in this spells and makes Temporal Sympathy therefore irrelevant. So basically: it works with all Time spells, but most written out Time spells simply don't need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't Rend Lifespan interact with a subject with weaker than Unchanged Temporal Sympathy with its present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:50:41-07:00","id":938946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938875#post938875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing about <i>specific</i> spells.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Spells <i>that call for it</i>&amp;quot; is a wider net than &amp;quot;'only' a quarter of the printed example spells for the Arcanum and no others.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? What other spells call for Temporal Sympathy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:27:43-07:00","id":939083,"title":"","content":"Space has three standard dimensions, where as time only has one dimension and can only run on one axis. Until you get to SpaceTimeSix <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kgEUdfX9WEU\" data-code=\"kgEUdfX9WEU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kgEUdfX9WEU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:08:33-07:00","id":939322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=938927#post938927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, are there any spells that <i>nonspecifically</i> call for Temporal Sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't pull this sarcastic semantics argument because I take issue with your not-uncontentious claim that <i>literally six spells at all and no others not attached to them</i> are the only viable core subjects for Temporal Sympathy post-erratum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fail to see how Momentary Flux or Postcognition would cause ripples in Time Sight, since they don't change the past in any way, but they can still be cast on subjects in the past with Temporal Sympathy. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the reason for that failure is simple:<br /> <br /> You're conflating a point I'm making about Temporal Sympathy not being able to send isolated spell effects back in time with any application of Temporal Sympathy at all, despite nobody in this discussion actually making the claim that using Temporal Sympathy to gather information was ever problematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Casting Rend Lifespan on someone in the past would certainly create ripples, but it isn't able to be cast on a subject in the past with Temporal Sympathy. </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rewrite History would certainly create ripples, and it can be used on a subject in the past without Temporal Sympathy as long as the subject has Unchanged Sympathy with its present self, but does require it if the Sympathy is any weaker. </div> </div> </div>Rewrite History isn't changing common history outside the scope of its subjects' timelines, much like Temporal Summoning isn't actually yanking the subject's past self out of the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shifting Sands is actual time travel but doesn't require Temporal Sympathy. </div> </div> </div>And rewinds you a semifixed distance from the present, either by less than a minute or in an increasingly bug-prone hour-by-hour arrangement, neither of which really <i>engages with</i> Temporal Sympathy in the sense of &quot;the weight of history has built up around this point in time, so it's harder to interface with using Time magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corridors of Time is actual time travel that does require Temporal Sympathy if the subject has weaker than Unchanged Temporal Sympathy with itself at the time you send it back to. </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Web-Weaver isn't even a Time spell but can be used on subjects in the past with Temporal Sympathy and without being combined with a Time spell. </div> </div> </div>You'll notice that the spell uses Temporal Sympathy to circumvent the need for current physical contact rather than to create a sympathetic connection <i>in the past</i>, which <i>would</i> create ripples on account of how spatial sympathy works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the quality of a spell that allows it to qualify for Temporal Sympathy is obvious to you, but you have consistently demonstrated a far better intuitive grasp of rules interactions than the average CofD fan. </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you want to use magic to change the past as experienced by people other than the specific targets of a spell, you cannot just shunt a spell you know into the past and must instead move yourself to a point prior to the spell's intended chronological point of origin and cast the spell you want to use&quot; is neither complicated nor contradicted by the state of affairs implied by the set of example spells that use Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> If you want to change The Past with magic, you yourself have to go there and do magic. Straightforward enough, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:39:46-07:00","id":939334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't pull this sarcastic semantics argument because I take issue with your not-uncontentious claim that <i>literally six spells at all and no others not attached to them</i> are the only viable core subjects for Temporal Sympathy post-erratum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. If you can point out other spells that can be affected by it, please do. If your point is that Temporal Sympathy can affect Creative spells, fine, but I don't believe the guidelines for how to decide if a creative spell should qualify for Temporal Sympathy are spelled out well enough for that argument to be compelling to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and the reason for that failure is simple:<br /> <br /> You're conflating a point I'm making about Temporal Sympathy not being able to send isolated spell effects back in time with any application of Temporal Sympathy at all, despite nobody in this discussion actually making the claim that using Temporal Sympathy to gather information was ever problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Momentary Flux and Postcognition not isolated spell effects? I'm honestly not understanding the distinction you're drawing here. I'm legitimately trying to get a better understanding of when Temporal Sympathy should be applicable to a spell and this part of your comment is really not helping me in that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rewrite History isn't changing common history outside the scope of its subjects' timelines, much like Temporal Summoning isn't actually yanking the subject's past self out of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, and so that is the reason it can be affected by Temporal Sympathy? I'm not getting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And rewinds you a semifixed distance from the present, either by less than a minute or in an increasingly bug-prone hour-by-hour arrangement, neither of which really <i>engages with</i> Temporal Sympathy in the sense of &quot;the weight of history has built up around this point in time, so it's harder to interface with using Time magic.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does it not engage with Temporal Sympathy in that sense? Why, if a character Awakened in the previous scene does sending them back to before they Awakend only require 1 Reach if you use Shifting Sands but requires the whole rigmarole of using Temporal Sympathy at a Weak Sympathetic Link if you do it with Corridors of Time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice that the spell uses Temporal Sympathy to circumvent the need for current physical contact rather than to create a sympathetic connection <i>in the past</i>, which <i>would</i> create ripples on account of how spatial sympathy works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If you want to use magic to change the past as experienced by people other than the specific targets of a spell, you cannot just shunt a spell you know into the past and must instead move yourself to a point prior to the spell's intended chronological point of origin and cast the spell you want to use&quot; is neither complicated nor contradicted by the state of affairs implied by the set of example spells that use Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> If you want to change The Past with magic, you yourself have to go there and do magic. Straightforward enough, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'll buy that. Then, what spells <i>can</i> Temporal Sympathy be applied to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:24:11-07:00","id":939350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939322#post939322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't pull this sarcastic semantics argument because I take issue with your not-uncontentious claim that <i>literally six spells at all and no others not attached to them</i> are the only viable core subjects for Temporal Sympathy post-erratum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel, are you aware that on another forum, Dave literally said that only spells that call for Temporal Sympathy in the description are affected by it? The fact that that was followed by this errata makes the reality super clear. You can yell semantics all you want, that was absolutely the intent here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/#47588918\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/#q47588918\" target=\"_blank\">47588918</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://ipv4.games/claim?name=fireden\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918\" target=\"_blank\"> 4chan archive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918\" target=\"_blank\"> https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 07-29-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:43:37-07:00","id":939360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939350#post939350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, are you aware that on another forum, Dave literally said that only spells that call for Temporal Sympathy in the description are affected by it? The fact that that was followed by this errata makes the reality super clear. You can yell semantics all you want, that was absolutely the intent here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be wrong here, but I'm pretty sure that what Satch is trying to express by objecting to my word choice is that Temporal Sympathy can be applied to appropriate Creative Thaumaturgy spells in addition to the 6 printed spells that call for it. Which I don't disagree with and never meant to counter-imply with my use of the word &quot;specific&quot;, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:49:28-07:00","id":939362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939360#post939360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could be wrong here, but I'm pretty sure that what Satch is trying to express by objecting to my word choice is that Temporal Sympathy can be applied to appropriate Creative Thaumaturgy spells in addition to the 6 printed spells that call for it. Which I don't disagree with and never meant to counter-imply with my use of the word &quot;specific&quot;, but whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I kind of assumed everyone figured that 'you can apply attainments to Creative Thaumaturgy' was a given for this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T23:02:27-07:00","id":939367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939334#post939334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Momentary Flux and Postcognition not isolated spell effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Momentary Flux and Postcognition <i>changing anything about the past</i>?<br /> <br /> The Future Is Unwritten means detecting scrutiny from the future (outside the context of &quot;someone has come to the past you inhabit and is scrutinizing you&quot;) is impossible and thus scrutiny of the past cannot affect the present in the same manner as wholesale time travel does.<br /> <br /> You can send a subject back in time through temporal sympathy because temporal sympathy is &quot;things have a connection to the way they used to be.&quot; <i>There is no &quot;used to be&quot; for spells</i>. Momentary Flux and Postcognition are spells that look at a point in time and do nothing else aside from maybe offering a vector for other investigatory spells to be used - Temporal Sympathy extends their range because it's basically pulling copies of established information forward, not because there's suddenly a Time Probe floating around in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly not understanding the distinction you're drawing here. I'm legitimately trying to get a better understanding of when Temporal Sympathy should be applicable to a spell and this part of your comment is really not helping me in that. </div> </div> </div>I have elsewhere repeated the sentiments of &quot;changing the past requires time travel&quot; and &quot;the mechanics for noticing when someone or something is trying to change the past through time travel do not exist purely for the purposes of ignoring them as you toss butterfly-effect bombs into the past from the present or are stopped by the ST from doing so through fiat alone&quot; and &quot;there is an entire section at the front of the Time Arcanum writeup before the description of Temporal Sympathy that frames time travel as a thing that moves a subject back to places it's already been and any spell you cast by definition has no sympathy with the time before you cast it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game takes place in the present, provides rules for going to the established past, and offers a quality of temporal magic that interacts with the notion that the past can be repeated in the present through memories and similar records. The more unfamiliar a point in the past is to its subject, the harder it is to bring that past to the subject or send the subject to that past; spells only properly exist within the span of their Duration, not after and not before, which means you can't cast a spell that starts before you actually cast it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, and so that is the reason it can be affected by Temporal Sympathy? I'm not getting it. </div> </div> </div>Altering someone's past necessarily involves looking at how much they've changed since a given point. Changing a person's life experience wholesale is necessarily more difficult than changing how they remember the last week and a half and no other quality supplies a more suitable Withstand rating for representing that particular aspect of the spell's scaling difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does it not engage with Temporal Sympathy in that sense? Why, if a character Awakened in the previous scene does sending them back to before they Awakend only require 1 Reach if you use Shifting Sands but requires the whole rigmarole of using Temporal Sympathy at a Weak Sympathetic Link if you do it with Corridors of Time? </div> </div> </div>You're relying on a particular reading of an extreme edge when there's a Time spell that specifically describes Unchanged sympathy as recent enough to be able to undo wounds and Conditions.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming that it's reasonable <i>to use</i> the Unmaking spell in a context where a Weaving spell is both sufficient to the task and still available to a Master. It requires the whole rigamarole because you specifically asked for a rigamarole<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure I follow. </div> </div> </div>Web-Weaver creates sympathetic ties as they are used by Space magic. The Time \u2022\u2022 addition to Web-Weaver does not send anything back in time. The addition modifies the spell's ability to generate a Weak sympathetic connection from physical contact <i>at the time of casting</i>, allowing the mage to instead upgrade a sympathetic tie from nonexistent to Weak if the target was in physical contact with a focal subject <i>during the time the caster is using temporal sympathy to</i>.<br /> <br /> You may notice that this has nothing to do with sending a spell effect back in time and everything to do with duplicating a past incidental sympathetic connection in the present, because sympathetic ties have consequences for the things they connect that will show up to Mage Sight at minimum and possibly alter history more drastically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, I'll buy that. Then, what spells <i>can</i> Temporal Sympathy be applied to? </div> </div> </div>Spells that look into the past, call forth or alter manifestations of a subject's past, or transport a subject to a point in their own past, in addition to spells to alter a subject's temporal sympathetic connections with its past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939350#post939350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, are you aware that on another forum, Dave literally said that only spells that call for Temporal Sympathy in the description are affected by it? The fact that that was followed by this errata makes the reality super clear. You can yell semantics all you want, that was absolutely the intent here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/#47588918\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/#q47588918\" target=\"_blank\">47588918</a><br /> <a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918\" target=\"_blank\">https://boards.fireden.net/tg/thread/47584806/47588918</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen that post, and it's depressing how apropos &quot;reader is making a special effort to be confused&quot; still is, because you're citing Dave's response to a claim that there's reasonable legitimate confusion between spatial and temporal sympathy just because both use the same word to describe the same type of umbrella concept as support for an argument that the erratum presented in this thread does anything other than clarify that you can't just apply Temporal Sympathy to any given spell effect you can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-29-2016, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T23:30:12-07:00","id":939375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Momentary Flux and Postcognition <i>changing anything about the past</i>?<br /> <br /> The Future Is Unwritten means detecting scrutiny from the future (outside the context of &quot;someone has come to the past you inhabit and is scrutinizing you&quot;) is impossible and thus scrutiny of the past cannot affect the present in the same manner as wholesale time travel does.<br /> <br /> You can send a subject back in time through temporal sympathy because temporal sympathy is &quot;things have a connection to the way they used to be.&quot; <i>There is no &quot;used to be&quot; for spells</i>. Momentary Flux and Postcognition are spells that look at a point in time and do nothing else aside from maybe offering a vector for other investigatory spells to be used - Temporal Sympathy extends their range because it's basically pulling copies of established information forward, not because there's suddenly a Time Probe floating around in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what &quot;used to be&quot; are they connecting to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have elsewhere repeated the sentiments of &quot;changing the past requires time travel&quot; and &quot;the mechanics for noticing when someone or something is trying to change the past through time travel do not exist purely for the purposes of ignoring them as you toss butterfly-effect bombs into the past from the present or are stopped by the ST from doing so through fiat alone&quot; and &quot;there is an entire section at the front of the Time Arcanum writeup before the description of Temporal Sympathy that frames time travel as a thing that moves a subject back to places it's already been and any spell you cast by definition has no sympathy with the time before you cast it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... Cool?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game takes place in the present, provides rules for going to the established past, and offers a quality of temporal magic that interacts with the notion that the past can be repeated in the present through memories and similar records. The more unfamiliar a point in the past is to its subject, the harder it is to bring that past to the subject or send the subject to that past; spells only properly exist within the span of their Duration, not after and not before, which means you can't cast a spell that starts before you actually cast it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll buy that argument for why you can't &quot;send spells back in time&quot;, but if Temporal Sympathy is a quality of temporal magic, why is an Attainment required to utilize that quality? Why isn't it just a system of penalties for recreating the past in the present based on how familiar that past is to the subject?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altering someone's past necessarily involves looking at how much they've changed since a given point. Changing a person's life experience wholesale is necessarily more difficult than changing how they remember the last week and a half and no other quality supplies a more suitable Withstand rating for representing that particular aspect of the spell's scaling difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, thank you for clarifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're relying on a particular reading of an extreme edge when there's a Time spell that specifically describes Unchanged sympathy as recent enough to be able to undo wounds and Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not relying on anything, I'm citing one of the reasons for my confusion as to what kinds of spells Temporal Sympathy is supposed to be applicable to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also assuming that it's reasonable <i>to use</i> the Unmaking spell in a context where a Weaving spell is both sufficient to the task and still available to a Master. It requires the whole rigamarole because you specifically asked for a rigamarole</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I don't see anything these spells are doing differently in the narrative beyond affecting points in time further into the past. Since Temporal Sympathy seems by my reading not to operate on how much time has passed but on how much the subject has changed, it seems odd to me that one would call for Temporal Sympathy and the other would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Web-Weaver creates sympathetic ties as they are used by Space magic. The Time \u2022\u2022 addition to Web-Weaver does not send anything back in time. The addition modifies the spell's ability to generate a Weak sympathetic connection from physical contact <i>at the time of casting</i>, allowing the mage to instead upgrade a sympathetic tie from nonexistent to Weak if the target was in physical contact with a focal subject <i>during the time the caster is using temporal sympathy to</i>.<br /> <br /> You may notice that this has nothing to do with sending a spell effect back in time and everything to do with duplicating a past incidental sympathetic connection in the present, because sympathetic ties have consequences for the things they connect that will show up to Mage Sight at minimum and possibly alter history more drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I <i>think</i> I get it? If this is the intent, I don't feel Temporal Sympathy was sufficiently explained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells that look into the past, call forth or alter manifestations of a subject's past, or transport a subject to a point in their own past, in addition to spells to alter a subject's temporal sympathetic connections with its past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. Can we just have the rules for Temporal Sympathy explain that instead of including specific allowances for Temporal Sympathy in the descriptions of spells on a case-by-case basis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:05:10-07:00","id":939384,"title":"","content":"I try to give some very boring but mechanical explanations to this:<br /> <br /> What Temporal Sympathy did before errata was basically time travel with every possible spell of every arcanum. This was either never meant to be or struck the developers as too difficult to handle.<br /> <br /> What Temporal Sympathy is doing now is giving you a possibility to influence the past of &quot;further away than unchanged&quot; subjects. In addition it is reducing the possibility of changing the past at all (no matter what connection you have to the past) to Time spells only. I think the latter one is VERY important and totally intentional. If you want to mess with the past, get good at time magic, it is not enough anymore to just get 2 dots in Time and do anything with it.<br /> <br /> To when you actually NEED Temporal Sympathy? Any time you want to interact (change, bring to the present or just watch) with anything from the past that is further away than unchanged connection. If you look at the Shifting Sands spell (which does not need Temporal Sympathy), I am extremely certain that this spell is not meant to bring you to a point of your own past, where you were changed! While this might theoretically be possible with a lot of reach, this is clearly not the intention of the spell. That is what Corridors of Time is for. You may also notice, that Corridors of Time doesn't need Temporal Sympathy if you want you put yourself a couple of days back in Time if you have not changed in that time period.<br /> <br /> So I suggest seeing the weaker than &quot;unchanged&quot; temporal connection as something as a veil, you have to pierce with Temporal Sympathy if needed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:36:19-07:00","id":939391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939375#post939375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what &quot;used to be&quot; are they connecting to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like a disconnect might be happening here, so attempting to proceed with clarity:<br /> <br /> The subject of the spells in question has a used-to-be, because that's what the spells are effectively pulling into the mage's present when they examine it. The spells themselves do not have a used-to-be, because they're spells that look back at a point on the established timeline rather than spells that exist in the past and look at a point in space.<br /> <br /> It's 3:30AM and metaphor is kind of fraught when it comes to talking about magic, but in short, the spells in question are rain dishes, not fishing rods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, I'll buy that argument for why you can't &quot;send spells back in time&quot;, but if Temporal Sympathy is a quality of temporal magic, why is an Attainment required to utilize that quality? </div> </div> </div>Because, much as Yantras became a thing partially to consolidate all the weird little disparate spellcasting bonuses that 1e had floating around under a cohesive umbrella, Arcanum Attainments became a thing partially to have a unified systems widget for the various &quot;at Arcanum X you gain this ability&quot; tricks that existed in 1e, like Unfettered and Counterspell and both varieties of sympathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why isn't it just a system of penalties for recreating the past in the present based on how familiar that past is to the subject? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how that would work and still interface with the spellcasting system without getting really untidy or having the system for Temporal Sympathy be an Attainment in all but name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but I don't see anything these spells are doing differently in the narrative beyond affecting points in time further into the past. Since Temporal Sympathy seems by my reading not to operate on how much time has passed but on how much the subject has changed, it seems odd to me that one would call for Temporal Sympathy and the other would not. </div> </div> </div>Shifting Sands is getting to your destination by running; Corridors of Time is calling in a helicopter. There's practically no shortcuts available to the former, but the latter takes some setup.<br /> <br /> Analogy notwithstanding, I'm reasonably certain that the example Weak temporal sympathy isn't talking about the immediate before-and-after difference of a mage Awakened freshly and without preamble in light of the other examples in the listing being fairly extensive processes of alteration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:25:14-07:00","id":939512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939391#post939391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a disconnect might be happening here, so attempting to proceed with clarity:</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939391#post939391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of the spells in question has a used-to-be, because that's what the spells are effectively pulling into the mage's present when they examine it. The spells themselves do not have a used-to-be, because they're spells that look back at a point on the established timeline rather than spells that exist in the past and look at a point in space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939391#post939391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, much as Yantras became a thing partially to consolidate all the weird little disparate spellcasting bonuses that 1e had floating around under a cohesive umbrella, Arcanum Attainments became a thing partially to have a unified systems widget for the various &amp;quot;at Arcanum X you gain this ability&amp;quot; tricks that existed in 1e, like Unfettered and Counterspell and both varieties of sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of them, though. Some were turned into Reach effects, and as Temporal Sympathy at current works on a spell-by-spell basis, I'm not convinced it wouldn't be better handled by Reach effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939391#post939391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how that would work and still interface with the spellcasting system without getting really untidy or having the system for Temporal Sympathy be an Attainment in all but name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty undidy right now. I think either decoupling Temporal Sympathy from individual spell descriptions or consigning it entirely to individual spell descriptions would be far tidier than the half-and-half approach we have now, which lead to a great deal of confusion about what exactly Temporal Sympathy is supposed to do and necessitated clarification in the errata that it only works when a spell says it's allowed to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939391#post939391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting Sands is getting to your destination by running; Corridors of Time is calling in a helicopter. There's practically no shortcuts available to the former, but the latter takes some setup.<br /> <br /> Analogy notwithstanding, I'm reasonably certain that the example Weak temporal sympathy isn't talking about the immediate before-and-after difference of a mage Awakened freshly and without preamble in light of the other examples in the listing being fairly extensive processes of alteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, it's weird that the metaphysics of Time care more about how much a subject has changed than about how much time has passed, unless you're casting Shifting Sands. It's inconsistent and muddies the issue of what exactly Temporal Sympathy <i>does</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:42:40-07:00","id":939528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I try to give some very boring but mechanical explanations to this:<br /> <br /> What Temporal Sympathy did before errata was basically time travel with every possible spell of every arcanum. This was either never meant to be or struck the developers as too difficult to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear from Dave's comments before the errata that his intent was never for Temporal Sympayhy to work that way. I also don't care, my position in this discussion has nothing to do with trying to preserve its former functionality, which <b>again</b>, I fully understand the decision to change and am not bothered by the loss of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Temporal Sympathy is doing now is giving you a possibility to influence the past of &amp;quot;further away than unchanged&amp;quot; subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, at least according to the way <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has been explaining it, which makes far more sense that this explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition it is reducing the possibility of changing the past at all (no matter what connection you have to the past) to Time spells only.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? There's an example Space spell that uses Temporal Sympathy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the latter one is VERY important and totally intentional. If you want to mess with the past, get good at time magic, it is not enough anymore to just get 2 dots in Time and do anything with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that was ever meant to be enough, and I am <i>still</i> not bothered by that fact. I am bothered by the design inelegance of an Attainment that requires spell descriptions to give it permission to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To when you actually NEED Temporal Sympathy? Any time you want to interact (change, bring to the present or just watch) with anything from the past that is further away than unchanged connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were the case (which <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has convinced me it's not), there would be no reason not to allow Temporal Sympathy to apply to, say, Rend Lifespan. Casting a damage spell on someone in the past with weaker than Unchanged Smpathy to the present is certainly inteacting with them, by way of changing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the Shifting Sands spell (which does not need Temporal Sympathy), I am extremely certain that this spell is not meant to bring you to a point of your own past, where you were changed! While this might theoretically be possible with a lot of reach, this is clearly not the intention of the spell. That is what Corridors of Time is for. You may also notice, that Corridors of Time doesn't need Temporal Sympathy if you want you put yourself a couple of days back in Time if you have not changed in that time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to say I think it's dumb that Shifting Sands works on chronological distance from the past when everything else in the Time arcanum works on metaphysical difference between the past and the present and leave it at that. This particular argument is extremely tangential to my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I suggest seeing the weaker than &amp;quot;unchanged&amp;quot; temporal connection as something as a veil, you have to pierce with Temporal Sympathy if needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go ahead and take <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>'s explanation over this one, as it's considerably more consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T16:46:03-07:00","id":939854,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about Incognito Presence having a Mana cost now. Does hiding from ghosts or cameras cost Mana as well? Giving a basic stealth spell a Mana cost seems strange to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T16:56:58-07:00","id":939859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939854#post939854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused about Incognito Presence having a Mana cost now. Does hiding from ghosts or cameras cost Mana as well? Giving a basic stealth spell a Mana cost seems strange to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's because its withstood only by the subject (tht is, if you cast it on an unwilling subject, them trying to be seen/heard anyway is how its withstood). It just makes everyone else ignore them by removing their mental &quot;presence&quot; in the world, the thing Mastigos call an aura.<br /> <br /> It is therefore an automatic success on any stealth actions the subject takes, and any attempt to spot them that isn't supernaturally powered automatically fails. <br /> <br /> Therefore, it costs Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:18:36-07:00","id":939866,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that logic put any kind of Veiling spell into 1 Mana category? If I cast Hidden Hoard on my treasure chest, any attempts that aren't supernaturally powered to find it automatically fail. I automatically succeed at my attempt to hide it (reversed Investigation, I guess?), while seekers automatically fail at their Investigations. Should it cost 1 Mana?<br /> Similarly, I cast Corpse Mask to hide cause of death, automatically succeeding at making it unrecognizable, and automatically foiling any attempts at discovering it. 1 Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:02:08-07:00","id":939901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939512#post939512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again though, it's weird that the metaphysics of Time care more about how much a subject has changed than about how much time has passed, unless you're casting Shifting Sands. It's inconsistent and muddies the issue of what exactly Temporal Sympathy <i>does</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space also has a weird metaphyics surrounding it. It cares less for the distance between two thing and more for the simular/symbolic distance. Like the bond between a parent and child is a strong bond no matter the actual distance between the two. I feel thi was a narrative move, which Im cool with.It also plays into the idea that our thought structures of distance and the passing of time are merely subjective and possible false. Quote the Lie. Which raises the question that prehaps the Superal realms are not as far off as orginally speculated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:18:52-07:00","id":939906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939901#post939901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space also has a weird metaphyics surrounding it. It cares less for the distance between two thing and more for the simular/symbolic distance. Like the bond between a parent and child is a strong bond no matter the actual distance between the two. I feel thi was a narrative move, which Im cool with.It also plays into the idea that our thought structures of distance and the passing of time are merely subjective and possible false. Quote the Lie. Which raises the question that prehaps the Superal realms are not as far off as orginally speculated</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood the part of that I find weird. I like the way Temporal Sympathy normally works based on how much things have changed based on how much actual time has passed. I don't like that Shifting Sands doesn't work that way too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:33:18-07:00","id":939908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939906#post939906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misunderstood the part of that I find weird. I like the way Temporal Sympathy normally works based on how much things have changed based on how much actual time has passed. I don't like that Shifting Sands doesn't work that way too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair Dues, my apologive. I'll have to look that up when I got the chance. Don'thave the book on me at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:28:46-07:00","id":939932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939512#post939512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all of them, though. Some were turned into Reach effects, and as Temporal Sympathy at current works on a spell-by-spell basis, I'm not convinced it wouldn't be better handled by Reach effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It adds three different costs, one of which involves a particular allocation of spell factors and all of which are thematically-shifted duplicates of something that <i>is</i> an Attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again though, it's weird that the metaphysics of Time care more about how much a subject has changed than about how much time has passed, unless you're casting Shifting Sands. It's inconsistent and muddies the issue of what exactly Temporal Sympathy <i>does</i>. </div> </div> </div>The thing about Shifting Sands is that there's no Duration-based snapback, you don't inhabit even your near-past self, and the effects on &quot;undone&quot; spells are as near as the spell gets to interacting with Temporal Sympathy through the whole &quot;spells don't start existing before you cast them&quot; aspect.<br /> <br /> You're pushing your way backwards from the present rather than picking a point in the past and pulling yourself to it through a sympathetic tie, which is why the spell is so much less Reach-efficient than Corridors of Time for less immediate revisions of history.<br /> <br /> Fraying history as it settles may result in &quot;time travel&quot; in a superficially similar fashion to unmaking the established past, but as the errata make clear, one allows the subject to completely alter that branch of the decision tree their timeline branched down with the only remaining consequence of the original history being &quot;this course of events led a Master of Time to rewrite history&quot; and the other sends your altered self back in time to try to change things despite the scars the original timeline has still left on them.*<br /> <br /> * Is an eyepatch in-concept for a Guardian Order Tool, do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:34:22-07:00","id":939935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939932#post939932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Is an eyepatch in-concept for a Guardian Order Tool, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd count it as a veil, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T01:53:32-07:00","id":940005,"title":"","content":"Funny how 3 or so pages are almost solely dedicated to talk about Time and its attaintments :P<br /> <br /> But it is nice with some of the changes, however, I would really liked if they also had included the reasonings behind the changes. Like I can't see why Heighten Senses is a Unveiling practice since you aren't Unveiling something that is hidden within your Arcanum, you are enhancing something that is already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:23:26-07:00","id":940028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939859#post939859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's because its withstood only by the subject (tht is, if you cast it on an unwilling subject, them trying to be seen/heard anyway is how its withstood). It just makes everyone else ignore them by removing their mental &quot;presence&quot; in the world, the thing Mastigos call an aura.<br /> <br /> It is therefore an automatic success on any stealth actions the subject takes, and any attempt to spot them that isn't supernaturally powered automatically fails.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it costs Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939866#post939866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that logic put any kind of Veiling spell into 1 Mana category? If I cast Hidden Hoard on my treasure chest, any attempts that aren't supernaturally powered to find it automatically fail. I automatically succeed at my attempt to hide it (reversed Investigation, I guess?), while seekers automatically fail at their Investigations. Should it cost 1 Mana?<br /> Similarly, I cast Corpse Mask to hide cause of death, automatically succeeding at making it unrecognizable, and automatically foiling any attempts at discovering it. 1 Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>As WHW said. All Veiling spells work that way so why only Incognito Presence costs mana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:44:20-07:00","id":940033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939866#post939866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that logic put any kind of Veiling spell into 1 Mana category? If I cast Hidden Hoard on my treasure chest, any attempts that aren't supernaturally powered to find it automatically fail. I automatically succeed at my attempt to hide it (reversed Investigation, I guess?), while seekers automatically fail at their Investigations. Should it cost 1 Mana?<br /> Similarly, I cast Corpse Mask to hide cause of death, automatically succeeding at making it unrecognizable, and automatically foiling any attempts at discovering it. 1 Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think is so much that normal attempts are auto-failures (all Veiling spells work that way as you pointed out) as that it will allow a great advantage to act completely unnoticed to the target. The rest of the veiling spells are more limited (Veiling only certain qualities) or work only against certain types of scrutiny (like being undetectable only to machines, or ghosts, or whatever) while this one is a broad one in both parameters. A small tithe of Mana doesn't seem out of the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:01:11-07:00","id":940175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940005#post940005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I can't see why Heighten Senses is a Unveiling practice since you aren't Unveiling something that is hidden within your Arcanum, you are enhancing something that is already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unveiling reveals things to you that your mundane senses can't pick up on, that's what Heighten Senses does, so it becomes Unveiling. I could even make the argument that since your normal senses can't pick up on the things you can perceive with Heightened Senses then that information actually is hidden from you and thus Unveiling is appropriate. You could use Perfecting to achieve the same effect, but if you can do it more efficiently at a lower level then, eh, why not? Maybe if you came up with a Perfecting version it would have superior benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:47:16-07:00","id":940229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939859#post939859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's because its withstood only by the subject (that is, if you cast it on an unwilling subject, them trying to be seen/heard anyway is how its withstood). It just makes everyone else ignore them by removing their mental &quot;presence&quot; in the world, the thing Mastigos call an aura.<br /> <br /> It is therefore an automatic success on any stealth actions the subject takes, and any attempt to spot them that isn't supernaturally powered automatically fails.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it costs Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I completely misunderstood who was Withstanding it: I thought anyone who was trying to notice you needed a higher Resolve than your spell's Potency. &quot;Automatically win against anyone who doesn't have Auspex or Mage Sight or something up&quot; feels significantly more powerful, yeah. I might need to figure out how to CT a lesser version that works a bit more like Obfuscate 1, although I'm not sure how possible that would be as a spell that targets yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:40:44-07:00","id":940303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940175#post940175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unveiling reveals things to you that your mundane senses can't pick up on, that's what Heighten Senses does, so it becomes Unveiling. I could even make the argument that since your normal senses can't pick up on the things you can perceive with Heightened Senses then that information actually is hidden from you and thus Unveiling is appropriate. You could use Perfecting to achieve the same effect, but if you can do it more efficiently at a lower level then, eh, why not? Maybe if you came up with a Perfecting version it would have superior benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How are you Unveiling Forces with Life magic? You can't Unveil whats on the other side of wall with Mind, you can however Perfect your inteligence and predict what it might be using information you have. You can Rule or Perfect your senses to work better thus perceive forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:58:12-07:00","id":940312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940303#post940303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you Unveiling Forces with Life magic? You can't Unveil whats on the other side of wall with Mind, you can however Perfect your inteligence and predict what it might be using information you have. You can Rule or Perfect your senses to work better thus perceive forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how you think that Heightened Senses is Unveiling Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:22:09-07:00","id":940325,"title":"","content":"I'm not, but you seem to. <br /> <br /> One can only Unveil things that are under Arcana purview. I don't see sound under Life's purview but you say that you Unveil it with Heightened Senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-30-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T17:18:12-07:00","id":940350,"title":"","content":"One of you is saying &quot;I use my senses to gather information; gathering information is Unveiling, and I'm using my senses to do so, which falls under Life, so it's Unveiling Life&quot;, while other says &quot;No, Unveiling is pointing a finger about something under arcanum's purview and getting information about it, so making my senses stronger should fall under Perfecting Life&quot;.<br /> Basically, in this argument, in order to get more information from sensory input, you would have to get Unveiling Forces, because you are pointing at sensory input and wanting to get information about it, and Life doesn't give you direct authority about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:24:20-07:00","id":940448,"title":"","content":"Spells that you point at something under an arcanum's purview and gain information about it are <i>Knowing</i>. Unveiling spells literally enhance your senses (whether expanding your visual range to include thermal vision, or letting you see and hear ghosts, or whatever). Heightened Senses is practically the definition of an Unveiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 07-31-2016, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:59:31-07:00","id":940462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940325#post940325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not, but you seem to.<br /> <br /> One can only Unveil things that are under Arcana purview. I don't see sound under Life's purview but you say that you Unveil it with Heightened Senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one who mentioned Forces, not me, so let's not get confused on that point. Now, do you hear things with your ears? Yes. Are there things that fall under Life that have better hearing than humans? Yes. Thus using Life you can use an Unveiling technique to observe information (audio or otherwise) that other organisms could potentially perceive. Now, if you used Forces then you can also perceive things that are beyond the ability for things that fall under Life, and you can use Unveiling with Forces to derive sensory information that is the same as what you might be able to perceive via Heightened Senses. Let's not forget that many arcana can actually achieve the same or similar types of effects after all. You might want to argue that gaining sensory information that's similar to another organism via Life is Weaving (Transplanting a property of one organism onto another) and you could. On the other hand Unveiling deals with revealing information that isn't mundanely available to you, which is exactly what Heightened Senses accomplishes hence it can also be Unveiling. You can look at this as similar to the way in which different arcana can achieve similar results, but instead of arcana sometimes practices also can achieve similar results. Usually when using a higher Practice though it's not unreasonable to expect the effect to be more powerful than using a lower level result. For instance using a Weaving version might grant a Condition, or 8 again, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:00:49-07:00","id":940551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940175#post940175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unveiling reveals things to you that your mundane senses can't pick up on, that's what Heighten Senses does, so it becomes Unveiling. I could even make the argument that since your normal senses can't pick up on the things you can perceive with Heightened Senses then that information actually is hidden from you and thus Unveiling is appropriate. You could use Perfecting to achieve the same effect, but if you can do it more efficiently at a lower level then, eh, why not? Maybe if you came up with a Perfecting version it would have superior benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with you here, but that was probably clear from the begining. As I see it, Heighten Senses doesn't reveal things mundane senses can't percieve; it enhances mundane senses. But it sounds like its about how we interprete the pratices. But just to ask; what practice do you think the Force spell Zoom In should be? Should it remain a Ruling or changed to Unveiling since it works like Heighten Senses, except it only enhances sight....... Allot :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:32:32-07:00","id":940554,"title":"","content":"I don't have an opinion on this yet, so I just restated the statements invovled :P<br /> But I'm curious, how would you handle a Death spell meant to give the mage ability to see in through shadows? I didn't want to copy Nightvision, and I feel a spell like this should be definitely possible, but I wonder how people would do that.<br /> [The fact that Darkness Bombing is one of best tactics for Death has no relation to me actually wanting this spell :P]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:48:45-07:00","id":940556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940554#post940554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have an opinion on this yet, so I just restated the statements invovled :P<br /> But I'm curious, how would you handle a Death spell meant to give the mage ability to see in through shadows? I didn't want to copy Nightvision, and I feel a spell like this should be definitely possible, but I wonder how people would do that.<br /> [The fact that Darkness Bombing is one of best tactics for Death has no relation to me actually wanting this spell :P]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It could be a veiling death spell, hiding the shadows from the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:51:51-07:00","id":940557,"title":"","content":"In Matter and Fate spell examples we can see that Ruling Practice is more than capable of 8-again effect. But Heightened Senses is like most of Compeling spell by granting Potency in dice to a roll.<br /> <br /> I understand your point of view and I see that you understand mine. I just don't agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:57:41-07:00","id":940558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940556#post940556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It could be a veiling death spell, hiding the shadows from the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that. Its like Life Veiling humans in a crowd to see all the non-humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:10:43-07:00","id":940563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940554#post940554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm curious, how would you handle a Death spell meant to give the mage ability to see in through shadows? I didn't want to copy Nightvision, and I feel a spell like this should be definitely possible, but I wonder how people would do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since human vision is dependent on light, I would argue that shadows don't convey nearly as much data. However, if such a spell would enable detecting all darkness within an area a Mage would know the exact location of all objects by determining where darkness is absent. By the same token, they could detect sound by determining where silence is disrupted, or detect heat by determining where cold stops. Human beings would be tiny indistinct anomalies in an ocean of Darkness, Silence and Cold. In better illuminated environments, I would allow Death to detect people by their shadows, or living creatures by their dying cells. Death already touches on many other Arcana, but in a limited manner. I think information-gathering spells would work the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T05:56:42-07:00","id":940590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940551#post940551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with you here, but that was probably clear from the begining. As I see it, Heighten Senses doesn't reveal things mundane senses can't percieve; it enhances mundane senses. But it sounds like its about how we interprete the pratices. But just to ask; what practice do you think the Force spell Zoom In should be? Should it remain a Ruling or changed to Unveiling since it works like Heighten Senses, except it only enhances sight....... Allot :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Zoom In is explicitly manipulating light rather than just imparting information to your senses, much in the same way that Matter 2 can shape objects. That's why its ruling. The Unveiling spells in Forces manipulate the Mage's senses to heightened levels to be able to perceive instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:11:12-07:00","id":941199,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I was aiming for something that simply allows you to use Shadows as extensions of your senses (and call the spell WHISPERING SHADOWS or something creepy like that), or something that mimicks Darkvision (switch penalties from dark to bright, then spend a reach to negate them). But some of these suggestions are really cool.<br /> But, we had a game using new Paradox rule, and it REALLY changed stuff.<br /> <br /> Context: we were clearing an old vineyard that is destined to become our Sanctum. Of course, it's a place that was previously used by another Mage, and for whatever reason, it has Environmental Condition that kickstarts paradox in each spell; during first session each spell had base pool of 1 paradox, in first part of second one it was 2, and in second part it was 3.<br /> It meant that Paradox happened, and well, mentality shifted a lot:<br /> - people started using Releasing, because &quot;bestow a Condition on SPELLS SUBJECT&quot; is much less threatening than &quot;bestow a Condition on SPELL CASTER&quot; <br /> - on the other hand, a person who would normally Release a Paradox started Containing it, because subjects of her spell was someone she didn't want to hurt, so she kept Containing it and Containing and Containing<br /> It produced screeching-Owl eyed Mage (the girl who kept amassing Paradox Conditions), and created two Size 5 masses of wind that got mutated into dangerous small tornadoes. Amusingly, person who used these spells is a Matter 3 Moros who wanted to push things around using wind as a pseudo telekinesis, soooooooooooooooooooo...<br /> <br /> There is a lot of fun that can happen due to Paradox now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:45:54-07:00","id":941215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941199#post941199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I was aiming for something that simply allows you to use Shadows as extensions of your senses (and call the spell WHISPERING SHADOWS or something creepy like that), or something that mimicks Darkvision (switch penalties from dark to bright, then spend a reach to negate them). But some of these suggestions are really cool.<br /> But, we had a game using new Paradox rule, and it REALLY changed stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you eleborate what you want that spell to actually do? Because switching darkness to brighness and vice versa does not actually get you any different information. You can try that with pictures on a computer. The dark parts are bright afterwards, but it will still just be one bright spot instead of one dark spot. The darkvision you discribe is basically nightvision with reducing the overload you would get from bright spots. So simply amplify the signal you get and reduce the oversaturation.<br /> <br /> What might actually be really interesting is doing something close to darkfield microscopy, which would give you different information from what you regularely can see, but before I go into detail of that I would like to know what you actually aim for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T09:54:52-07:00","id":941233,"title":"","content":"I meant reversing being &quot;blinded&quot; by darkness and seeing in light to being &quot;blinded&quot; by light and seeing in darkness. I basically want a spell that allows me to comfortably work in the dark, and don't want to directly copy Darkvision from Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:03:32-07:00","id":941392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=940551#post940551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with you here, but that was probably clear from the begining. As I see it, Heighten Senses doesn't reveal things mundane senses can't percieve; it enhances mundane senses. But it sounds like its about how we interprete the pratices. But just to ask; what practice do you think the Force spell Zoom In should be? Should it remain a Ruling or changed to Unveiling since it works like Heighten Senses, except it only enhances sight....... Allot :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, here's another way to look at it maybe? When you cast the spell you're commanding Life to Unveil to you things that more sensitive organisms can detect. By mundane senses earlier I meant normal human senses by the way. It's fine if you still disagree, I'm just finding the conversation interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:24:20-07:00","id":941610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941233#post941233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant reversing being &quot;blinded&quot; by darkness and seeing in light to being &quot;blinded&quot; by light and seeing in darkness. I basically want a spell that allows me to comfortably work in the dark, and don't want to directly copy Darkvision from Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would try something like alteration to your eyes to be like a deep sea fish or your ears to pick up the sonic range like a bat for possible start point for a spell that does it using Life. Just an idea that you can dismiss or possibly run with. It probably wouldn't work as early dot wise as Forces but it'll work for any mage with a good understanding of the Life Arcanum (3 dots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 08-01-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:48:38-07:00","id":941622,"title":"","content":"That would just be Life Unveiling, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:22:51-07:00","id":941637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941622#post941622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would just be Life Unveiling, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, rock it Hon if your the ST or y our ST agrees. I feel it's totally doable but isn't easily done like a mage knowledgeable in Forces.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:43:15-07:00","id":941683,"title":"","content":"Yeah, any spell that physically alters qualities of your character's body without wholesale transformation is Life Weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:34:11-07:00","id":941726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941233#post941233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant reversing being &quot;blinded&quot; by darkness and seeing in light to being &quot;blinded&quot; by light and seeing in darkness. I basically want a spell that allows me to comfortably work in the dark, and don't want to directly copy Darkvision from Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that basically is &quot;Nightvision&quot;. Of course you can also use Life to change your eyes so that they are able to perceive the additional spectra and get more sensitiv, but there is no way around amplification for this.<br /> You might also go for some kind of Daredevil sense by imitation of the ultrasonic senses of bats, but that would be life too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T01:57:26-07:00","id":941771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941683#post941683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, any spell that physically alters qualities of your character's body without wholesale transformation is Life Weaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to alter a quality of your body though, just devise a spell that reveals what a bat or whatever would sense without actually weaving that ability into your Pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:02:37-07:00","id":941772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941771#post941771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to alter a quality of your body though, just devise a spell that reveals what a bat or whatever would sense without actually weaving that ability into your Pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>You finally convinced me to Heightened Senses being Unveiling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I mean the effect the spell can be made with Compelling, it just enhances it a little but borrowing senses of another animal without making bodily alterations is very cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:09:04-07:00","id":941857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941771#post941771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to alter a quality of your body though, just devise a spell that reveals what a bat or whatever would sense without actually weaving that ability into your Pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly disagree, because what the bat is actually &quot;hearing&quot; or the deep see fish &quot;sees&quot; is not under the purview of Life and can therefore not be unveiled with Life.<br /> <br /> Heightened Senses is still ruling, since you ramp up the sensitivity of your own senses. What Mrmdubois is discribing is a Forces spell similar to Nightvision, but for other forms of energy which can be used to percieve your surroundings. Like a spell to percieve ultra- or infrasound. You can, for example, not use this to get an improved sense of smell, but you could probably devise a matter spell, which lets you detect certain chemicals in the air, which would work like the nose of a dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-02-2016, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:14:14-07:00","id":941863,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about perceiving energy at all. I'm talking about how Heightened Senses makes sense as an Unveiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:48:34-07:00","id":941976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941863#post941863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about perceiving energy at all. I'm talking about how Heightened Senses makes sense as an Unveiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is actually a Ruling spell and it doesn't really make sense as an Unveiling spell at all. It is a Ruling spell because you amplify your own senses on a lower degree, otherwise it would be Perfecting.<br /> There is nothing to unveile here which is under the purview of Life as an arcanum. Sensory organs of animals do not percieve life but certain energy or chemicals. You probably could use an Unveiling spell on an actual bat to unveile what that bat is perceiving. But then you would need to have a bat with you at all times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:00:08-07:00","id":941986,"title":"","content":"If you look at the errata you'll see its in fact not a Ruling spell. So once you have correct information we can discuss this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:05:53-07:00","id":941991,"title":"","content":"The whole discussion is about how Heiightened Senses moved down from 2nd dot to 1st dot and changed practices, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:11:50-07:00","id":941996,"title":"","content":"Heightened Senses is a spell that explicitly <i>does not</i> grant new senses; merely improving the acuity of your existing ones. That can be handwaved through a number of ways, such as increasing a Mage's ability to perceive information more clearly or otherwise sort through existing perceptual inputs. It's not creating new data; merely making it easier to sift through existing information.<br /> <br /> Being able to echolocate or see miles away, however, are not something a human does. That outright requires new qualities. A Life Knowing or Unveiling spell can tell you a lot about an eagle's eyes but it can't give you them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:17:56-07:00","id":941999,"title":"","content":"That's about the same as saying that an Unveiling Forces spell can tell you a lot about radio waves but not able to perceive them or the information they're carrying. Which is patently not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:33:26-07:00","id":942012,"title":"","content":"It's really not. A Forces Unveiling spell reveals to you some aspect under the arcanum's purview, which radio waves fall under. Zoom In, meanwhile, requires active manipulation of the arcanum's purview and is, thus, a Ruling spell.<br /> <br /> A Life Unveiling or Knowing spell can tell you everything about things under Life's purview; detailing anything and everything about the living world around you. Actually granting senses you do not have, such as extreme distance vision or echolocation, aren't within Life's purview except as they exist as features of animal forms. Accessing them requires producing the feature that allows them via shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:45:19-07:00","id":942021,"title":"","content":"You do not need to have the eyes of an eagle to be able to determine what an eagle would see if it was looking at what you're looking at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:56:30-07:00","id":942028,"title":"","content":"Aside from stuff specifically in Life's wheelhouse? You do. Life knows eagle eyes; it doesn't know the things eagle eyes see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:59:26-07:00","id":942032,"title":"","content":"Eh, agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:06:52-07:00","id":942038,"title":"","content":"Yep. If it works in your games, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:44:47-07:00","id":942535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941986#post941986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the errata you'll see its in fact not a Ruling spell. So once you have correct information we can discuss this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I missed that. But anyway, my argument stands. Heightened Senses does not give you the vision of an eagle or the echolocation of a bat. It explicitely says so. The spell only improves the information you get from your existing senses. I can live with that in the way that the spell does not actually improve the sensory output your organs create (it does not give you the nose of a dog NOR the information the nose of a dog would get) but it improves your interpretation of the information your existing sensory organs get. Some blind people develope astonishingly good sense of hearing for example and I can see how this is Unveiling instead of ruling.<br /> <br /> However Heightened Senses does not give you any information you simply cannot percieve with your own senses. The spell explicitely says that it does not grant new senses. So you don't get nightvision, or echolocation or infrasound or anything like this from the spell at all. And of course it is possible to determine what an eagle would see, but not with Life. To do this, you must know what is actually the difference between an eagles eyes and a humans (percieving 150 images/s, ultraviolet light, faster focusing and so on) and develope a spell that does percieve this information.<br /> <br /> While I guess, we still agree to disagree, I at least wanted to make my argument clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:44:29-07:00","id":942572,"title":"","content":"I didn't say it did, those were examples for the kinds of ways senses can be enhanced via Life and why Heightened Senses thus makes sense as Unveiling. You really gotta start paying better attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:43:33-07:00","id":942653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941392#post941392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, here's another way to look at it maybe? When you cast the spell you're commanding Life to Unveil to you things that more sensitive organisms can detect. By mundane senses earlier I meant normal human senses by the way. It's fine if you still disagree, I'm just finding the conversation interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did pay attention and you did write this. And this is exactly what I disagree upon. Using an Unveiling Life spell to make more out of your own senses (Heightened Senses) I can agree with. Using an Unveiling Life spell to give you information about what a more sensitive organism <i>would </i>probably see is not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T06:06:40-07:00","id":942662,"title":"","content":"What about plugging into the Force...I mean, All Life Around You and asking it a question &quot;hey, can you help me see it&quot;? It's not a question of &quot;what would they see&quot;, but of &quot;Life asks life-forms what they see, and gives you their feedback in understandable manner&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T07:01:53-07:00","id":942686,"title":"","content":"That would probably be a combination of Mind and Life, but that might be up for discussion. In any way I am ok with that, since the information of what that crow in your garden sees is actually present and can sensibly be made accessible by unveiling magic. But the abstract concept of what a crow, which is not present, <i>would </i>see is pretty much a Making spell since it is creating something (sensory information) out of nothingness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:04:14-07:00","id":942979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=942686#post942686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would probably be a combination of Mind and Life, but that might be up for discussion. In any way I am ok with that, since the information of what that crow in your garden sees is actually present and can sensibly be made accessible by unveiling magic. But the abstract concept of what a crow, which is not present, <i>would </i>see is pretty much a Making spell since it is creating something (sensory information) out of nothingness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's just ridiculous. You're not creating the sensory information itself, nor would you need a crow to be present for you to gain it's senses; transforming your body is capable of doing that. Furthermore, extra sensory perception is quite literally under the purview of the unveiling practice. You want to rule that it takes a weaving or ruling spell to do this if the thing being sensed isnt under the purview of Life, sure, go ahead. But don't be silly and say that it takes making. Creating the phenomena under the purview of a particular arcanum would be making, but sensing something under it's purview is unveiling. If it's not under the purview of Life, at most it would take a weaving spell to change your senses to perceive what you're trying to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:12:19-07:00","id":943435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941392#post941392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, here's another way to look at it maybe? When you cast the spell you're commanding Life to Unveil to you things that more sensitive organisms can detect. By mundane senses earlier I meant normal human senses by the way. It's fine if you still disagree, I'm just finding the conversation interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good way of writting it, makes it sound much more like an Unveiling spell. I am still however, not completly convinced, though changing the description of a spell really helps define what practice it is, and I would accept yours in my game because it is so close to explain it.. And I don't want to be to nid picky <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, with this huge amount of posts about Heighten Senses, I feel like I have opened up ssomethin akind to Pandora's Forum :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:26:48-07:00","id":943441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=942979#post942979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that's just ridiculous. You're not creating the sensory information itself, nor would you need a crow to be present for you to gain it's senses; transforming your body is capable of doing that. Furthermore, extra sensory perception is quite literally under the purview of the unveiling practice. You want to rule that it takes a weaving or ruling spell to do this if the thing being sensed isnt under the purview of Life, sure, go ahead. But don't be silly and say that it takes making. Creating the phenomena under the purview of a particular arcanum would be making, but sensing something under it's purview is unveiling. If it's not under the purview of Life, at most it would take a weaving spell to change your senses to perceive what you're trying to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read the whole discussion. Sensing ultrasound is not under the purview of Life. You can easily do this with Forces Unveiling. I never argued against this. Mrmdubois on the other hand said that you can use Life Unveiling to get sensory information that a bat would perceive if a bat was present. While the ultrasound the bat would be using is present and can be unveiled with Forces, the information what a hypothetical bat would see is NOT present. To get this information <i>without</i> transforming yourself you would literally have to create the sensory organs of a bat, which are under the purview of Life, and then take information out of them. Or you could just transform yourself, which is still not Unveiling.<br /> With the same internal logic I could use Prime or Spirit Unveiling to create the Information of what a Cherubim or a Spirit God <i>would</i> see if it was present and simply pierce any Mysterium right ahead.<br /> <br /> Again: I am totally fine with Heightened Senses beeing Unveiling, but it does not work this way:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=941392#post941392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, here's another way to look at it maybe? When you cast the spell you're commanding Life to Unveil to you things that more sensitive organisms can detect. By mundane senses earlier I meant normal human senses by the way. It's fine if you still disagree, I'm just finding the conversation interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:35:52-07:00","id":943744,"title":"","content":"So, about the combined spells - what if I combine two spell with different primary factors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:42:01-07:00","id":943747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=943744#post943744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, about the combined spells - what if I combine two spell with different primary factors?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was surprised not to see anything about this in the errata. I'm sure the general idea here is to just pick one.<br /> Our group lets the combined spell have both, but that's probably broken-overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:11:48-07:00","id":943765,"title":"","content":"You could rule that combining spells requires matched primary factors. Easy patch to include or not. (Still digesting the book, as I just got it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:21:03-07:00","id":943772,"title":"","content":"We assumed that you need to &quot;fix&quot; the spell by applying a Reach to make all components use the same primary factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:53:09-07:00","id":943794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=943772#post943772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We assumed that you need to &quot;fix&quot; the spell by applying a Reach to make all components use the same primary factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good take, too. I like it much better than 'pick one'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:20:20-07:00","id":943871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=943441#post943441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please read the whole discussion. Sensing ultrasound is not under the purview of Life. You can easily do this with Forces Unveiling. I never argued against this. Mrmdubois on the other hand said that you can use Life Unveiling to get sensory information that a bat would perceive if a bat was present. While the ultrasound the bat would be using is present and can be unveiled with Forces, the information what a hypothetical bat would see is NOT present. To get this information <i>without</i> transforming yourself you would literally have to create the sensory organs of a bat, which are under the purview of Life, and then take information out of them. Or you could just transform yourself, which is still not Unveiling.<br /> With the same internal logic I could use Prime or Spirit Unveiling to create the Information of what a Cherubim or a Spirit God <i>would</i> see if it was present and simply pierce any Mysterium right ahead.<br /> <br /> Again: I am totally fine with Heightened Senses beeing Unveiling, but it does not work this way:</div> </div> </div> </div>I HAVE read the whole discussion. And in so doing I found this little tidbit where you presented the absurd idea that a mage would have to be a master of life in order to sense what a hypothetical animal could sense because you believe he would have to actually create the sensory information itself. I further went on to say that if you wanted to rule such sensory information as being outside the purview of Life, then fair enough, but at highest it would only require a weaving spell to find out what said information was, NOT making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}